window.BOOKS.push({"id":"traps-zaps","kind":"items","title":"Chess Openings: Traps and Zaps","author":"Bruce Pandolfini","color":"#5b3f8c","glyph":"♝","level":"Opening traps","about":"Short games where one side falls into a trap in the opening. Find the move that punishes it, then read why the mistake happened.","items":[{"id":"T1","q":"1","title":"Trap 1","page":3,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/ppppbppp/5n2/4P1B1/3Q4/8/PPP2PPP/RN2KBNR b KQkq - 0 5","line":["Nc6"],"cp":268,"need":1,"lesson":"White pushed his e-pawn to attack the knight instead of developing his pieces. Black's knight jumps out with a threat on the Queen, and White's lonely Queen and pawn get into trouble.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nf6 4.Bg5 Be7 5.e5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T2","q":"2","title":"Trap 2","page":4,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kb1r/ppp2ppp/2n2n2/6B1/Q3q3/8/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 0 9","line":["Rd8+","Kxd8"],"cp":297,"need":1,"lesson":"Black grabbed a piece while his King was still in the center and thought his Queen was safe. He forgot to check White's Rook check, which pulls the King away and leaves the knight pinned so it can't protect the Queen.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nc6 4.Qa4 Nf6 5.Nc3 d5 6.Bg5 dxe4 7.Nxe4 Qe7 8.O-O-O Qxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T3","q":"3","title":"Trap 3","page":5,"type":"mate","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp1np1p/2np2p1/3N4/4P3/2B1Q3/P1P1NPPP/b3KB1R w Kkq - 0 10","line":["Nf6+","Kf8","Qh6#"],"mate":2,"need":3,"lesson":"Black traded away his dark-square Bishop just to grab a Rook. Without that Bishop, the dark squares f6 and h6 around his King had no defender, and White mated there.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nc6 4.Qe3 g6 5.Nc3 Bg7 6.Nd5 Nge7 7.Ne2 d6 8.Bd2 Bxb2 9.Bc3 Bxa1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T4","q":"4","title":"Trap 4","page":6,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/pppp1ppp/2n3n1/b7/2B1P2P/2P3Q1/PP3PP1/RNB1K1NR w KQ - 1 9","line":["h5","Qe8","hxg6","Qxe4+","Be2","Qxg6","Qxg6","hxg6","Nd2","d6","Ngf3","Bg4"],"cp":297,"need":3,"lesson":"Black sent his Bishop far away and put his knight on a poor square, then castled right into White's attack. White's h-pawn, Rook and dark-square Bishop crashed through the weak squares near Black's King.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nc6 4.Qe3 Bb4+ 5.c3 Ba5 6.Bc4 Nge7 7.Qg3 O-O 8.h4 Ng6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T5","q":"5","title":"Trap 5","page":7,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/5n2/2b1n3/4P3/1BP3Q1/PP3PPP/RNB1K1NR b KQkq - 2 8","line":["Bxf2+","Kxf2"],"cp":862,"need":1,"lesson":"White kept moving his Queen around for no good reason and left the d3 square without a pawn guard. Black sacrificed a Bishop to pull White's King or Queen onto a square where a knight could fork them both.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nc6 4.Qe3 Nf6 5.Bc4 Ne5 6.Bb3 Bb4+ 7.c3 Bc5 8.Qg3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T6","q":"6","title":"Trap 6","page":8,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp1bppp/8/3N4/8/4Q3/nPPB1PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 0 10","line":["Kb1"],"cp":152,"need":1,"lesson":"Black got greedy and grabbed a far-away pawn with his knight while his King was still in the center. Simply taking back on d5 would have kept him fine, but now White's pieces could strike at his King.","intro":"Center Game. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Qxd4 Nc6 4.Qe3 Nf6 5.Nc3 Be7 6.Bd2 d5 7.exd5 Nb4 8.O-O-O Nfxd5 9.Nxd5 Nxa2+. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Game","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T7","q":"7","title":"Trap 7","page":9,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1k1nr/pppp1ppp/8/2b4q/2B1P3/2P2N2/P3QPPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 3 8","line":["g4","Qh3"],"cp":191,"need":1,"lesson":"Black brought his Queen out early and then parked her on the edge of the board, where she had few escape squares. White chased her with pawns and pieces until she was trapped.","intro":"Center Gambit. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Bc4 Qh4 4.Qe2 Bb4+ 5.c3 dxc3 6.bxc3 Bc5 7.Nf3 Qh5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Gambit","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T8","q":"8","title":"Trap 8","page":10,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1k1nr/ppp2ppp/6q1/2bB2B1/4P3/2P2N2/P4PPP/RN1QK2R w KQkq - 3 9","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Ne5+","Kf8","Nxg6+","hxg6","Qd8+","Kf7","Qxc8","Be7","Qxb7","Nd7"],"cp":1474,"need":5,"lesson":"Black kept moving his Bishop and Queen instead of developing his knights. White's pieces were all out and ready, so they swarmed Black's King and checkmated it.","intro":"Center Gambit. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.Nf3 Bb4+ 4.c3 dxc3 5.bxc3 Bc5 6.Bc4 d5 7.Bxd5 Qf6 8.Bg5 Qg6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Center Gambit","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T9","q":"9","title":"Trap 9","page":11,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk1nr/ppppbppp/8/8/2B1P3/2P5/P4PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6","line":["Qd5","Nh6","Bxh6","O-O","Be3","d6","Qd3","Nd7","Nf3","Bf6","g3","Qe8"],"cp":197,"need":3,"lesson":"Black put his Bishop on e7, which blocked the square his Queen needed to protect f7. White aimed his Queen and Bishop at f7, and Black could not defend it.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 Bb4 5.bxc3 Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T10","q":"10","title":"Trap 10","page":12,"type":"play","fen":"rn1qk2r/pppb1ppp/5n2/1B1pP3/1b6/8/PB3PPP/RN1Q1KNR w kq - 2 9","line":["Qa4","Ne4","Qxb4","c5","Qb3","O-O","Bxd7","Qxd7","Nf3","Kh8","Qc2","Nc6"],"cp":-16,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black grabbed pawns and made a pointless Bishop check instead of developing and keeping his pieces safe. White's Queen then attacked two loose Black pieces at once.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 Bb4+ 6.Kf1 Nf6 7.e5 d5 8.Bb5+ Bd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T11","q":"11","title":"Trap 11","page":13,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/pppn1ppp/8/1B1pP3/1b6/8/PB3PPP/RN1Q1KNR w kq - 2 9","line":["e6","fxe6"],"cp":-12,"alt":["Qg4","Qg4"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black tried to keep all the pawns he grabbed while his pieces stayed undeveloped. Pointless checks left his King and pieces open to White's well-developed army.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 Bb4+ 6.Kf1 Nf6 7.e5 d5 8.Bb5+ Nfd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T12","q":"12","title":"Trap 12","page":14,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kb1r/ppp1qppp/5n2/3pP3/2B5/8/PB2QPPP/RN2K1NR w KQkq d6 0 8","line":["exf6","Qxe2+","Bxe2","gxf6","h4","Rg8","Kf1","Nc6","Nf3","Be7","Nbd2"],"cp":202,"need":3,"lesson":"Black thought trading Queens would let him win White's Bishop, but the trade itself moved the Bishop to safety. Look at each new position fresh instead of trusting what you planned a move ago.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Saving by Capturing. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 Nf6 6.e5 Qe7 7.Qe2 d5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Saving by Capturing"},{"id":"T13","q":"13","title":"Trap 13","page":15,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pppp1ppp/8/8/2B5/2B5/P4PPP/R2Q1RK1 w - - 1 11","line":["Qg4","Qf6","Bxf6","g6","Qh3","h5","Qc3","d5","Bxd5","Nd7","Bg7"],"cp":1179,"need":3,"lesson":"Black grabbed one pawn too many and left his King facing White's Queen and Bishops. Giving a pawn back to finish developing would have been much safer.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 Nf6 6.Nc3 Bb4 7.Ne2 Nxe4 8.O-O Nxc3 9.Nxc3 Bxc3 10.Bxc3 O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T14","q":"14","title":"Trap 14","page":16,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p5/3N4/4P3/8/PB3PPP/R2QK1NR w KQkq - 0 9","line":["Nf6+","gxf6","Qxd8+","Kxd8","Bxf6+","Ke8","O-O-O","Be7","Bxh8","Be6","Nf3","Nd7"],"cp":188,"need":3,"lesson":"Black wasted a move pushing a pawn to chase White's Knight when he needed to develop a new piece. White used that lost time to fork the King and Rook.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 d5 6.Bxd5 Nf6 7.Nc3 Nxd5 8.Nxd5 c6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T15","q":"15","title":"Trap 15","page":17,"type":"play","fen":"rn1qkb1r/ppp3pp/3p1n2/8/4P1N1/8/PB3PPP/RN1QK2R w KQ - 1 10","line":["Nxf6+"],"cp":733,"need":1,"lesson":"Black grabbed pawns and brought out his Bishop before his Knights, so he could not castle. His King got stuck in the open and his Queen was skewered behind it.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 d6 6.Nf3 Bg4 7.Bxf7+ Kxf7 8.Ne5+ Ke8 9.Nxg4 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T16","q":"16","title":"Trap 16","page":18,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k1nr/pppp1pQp/2n2q2/8/1b2P3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 1 7","line":["Bh6","Nd4","Qxf6","Nxf6","O-O-O","Ne6","f3","Bxc3","bxc3","d6","Ne2","Nc5"],"cp":125,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black moved his Bishop out early instead of developing a Knight, which let White's Queen grab the g7 pawn. The empty g7 square became a home for White's Queen and Bishop.","intro":"Danish Gambit. Theme: Deflection. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.d4 exd4 3.c3 dxc3 4.Nxc3 Bb4 5.Qd4 Nc6 6.Qxg7 Qf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Danish Gambit","tactic":"Deflection"},{"id":"T17","q":"17","title":"Trap 17","page":19,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/2n5/4P3/1bB1n3/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 1 8","line":["Qd5","Qe7","Qxe4","d6","O-O","Bxc3","bxc3","Nxe5","Nxe5","Qxe5","Re1","Qxe4"],"cp":358,"need":3,"lesson":"Black put his Knight on e4 where nothing protected it. White's Queen then threatened mate on f7 and the loose Knight at the same time.","intro":"Goring Gambit. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.c3 dxc3 5.Nxc3 Bb4 6.Bc4 Nf6 7.e5 Ne4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Goring Gambit","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T18","q":"18","title":"Trap 18","page":20,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k1nr/pppq1ppp/3p4/n1bN4/2B1P3/1Q3N2/PP3PPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 4 9","line":["Qc3","Nf6"],"cp":399,"need":1,"lesson":"Black's Knight went to the edge where it was unprotected, and his g7 pawn was left unguarded. Don't start fights before your pieces are developed and your King is safe.","intro":"Goring Gambit. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.c3 dxc3 5.Nxc3 Bc5 6.Bc4 d6 7.Qb3 Qd7 8.Nd5 Na5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Goring Gambit","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T19","q":"19","title":"Trap 19","page":21,"type":"playout","fen":"r1bq1bnr/pppp2pp/2n1k3/4N3/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 1 8","line":["Qd5+","Ke7","Qf7+","Kd6","Nc4+","Kc5","Qd5+","Kb4","a3+","Ka4","b3#"],"mate":6,"goal":"mate","lesson":"Black moved the same Knight three times and wasted time while his King walked into the middle. A King without its army around it gets hunted down.","intro":"Scotch Gambit. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Bc4 Na5 5.Bxf7+ Kxf7 6.Ne5+ Ke6 7.Qxd4 Nc6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Gambit","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T20","q":"20","title":"Trap 20","page":22,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/7n/2b1n1NQ/2BpP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 6 7","line":["Ne6","dxe6","Qxe5","Qh4","Qxc5","Qxe4+","Kf1","Bd7","Nd2","Qxc2","Kg1","d3"],"cp":181,"need":5,"lesson":"Black moved a Knight that was already out instead of bringing out a new piece like the Queen to e7. Every move counts in the opening, so try to develop a different piece each turn.","intro":"Scotch Gambit. Theme: Multiple Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Bc4 Bc5 5.Ng5 Nh6 6.Qh5 Ne5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Gambit","tactic":"Multiple Attack"},{"id":"T21","q":"21","title":"Trap 21","page":23,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2pp1/1b5p/3nn3/3pN3/1B5P/PPP2PP1/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 11","line":["Qh5","Qe7","Bxd5","d3","cxd3","c6","Bb3","Nxd3","Qf3"],"cp":324,"need":3,"lesson":"Putting the Knight on e7 left f7 weak and the Black pieces loose with the King still in the middle. White's Queen attacked a Knight that was pinned to the King.","intro":"Scotch Gambit. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Bc4 Bc5 5.O-O Nge7 6.Ng5 d5 7.exd5 Ne5 8.Bb3 h6 9.Ne4 Bb6 10.h3 Nxd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Gambit","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T22","q":"22","title":"Trap 22","page":24,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k1nr/ppp2pp1/3p1q1p/2b1n1NQ/3pPP2/1B6/PPP3PP/RNB2RK1 b kq f3 0 9","line":["d3+","Kh1"],"cp":574,"need":1,"lesson":"White forgot about Black's Bishop aiming at his King and thought his Knight on g5 was safe. Opening rules are guides, not laws, so always check what your opponent is threatening.","intro":"Scotch Gambit. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Bc4 Bc5 5.O-O d6 6.Ng5 Ne5 7.Bb3 h6 8.Qh5 Qf6 9.f4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Gambit","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T23","q":"23","title":"Trap 23","page":25,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppppnp1p/2n3p1/3N2B1/3bP3/8/PPP2PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["Qxd4","O-O","Nf6+","Kh8","Qc3","Ne5","Qxe5","d6"],"cp":796,"need":1,"lesson":"Black traded away his dark-square Bishop, the piece that guarded the squares around his King. White's pieces then moved into f6 and h6 for checkmate.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Nge7 5.Nc3 g6 6.Bg5 Bg7 7.Nd5 Bxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T24","q":"24","title":"Trap 24","page":26,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/p1pbbppp/1p3n2/1B1pP3/3Q1P2/8/PPP3PP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 2 11","line":["exf6","Bxb5","fxe7","Qxe7","Rd1","O-O-O","Nc3","Bc6","a4","Qf6","Qxf6","gxf6"],"cp":349,"need":3,"lesson":"Black moved the same pieces twice and pushed pawns instead of castling. Time is what counts in the opening, and wasting it lets your opponent attack.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Promotion. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Be7 5.Bc4 Nf6 6.O-O Nxd4 7.Qxd4 d6 8.f4 b6 9.e5 d5 10.Bb5+ Bd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Promotion"},{"id":"T25","q":"25","title":"Trap 25","page":27,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/5N1q/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 5 7","line":["Be2","Qg6","Nh4","Qxe4","Nxe4","Nxe4","Bf3","Nc5","b4","Ne6","c3","d6"],"cp":784,"need":5,"lesson":"Black brought his Queen out early and then blocked her escape route with his own Knight. If you take the Queen out early, you have to be extra careful she can't get trapped.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Qh4 5.Nc3 Nf6 6.Nf5 Qh5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T26","q":"26","title":"Trap 26","page":28,"type":"play","fen":"N1bkr3/pp1p1ppp/2n5/2b5/4n2q/3B1Q2/PPP2PPP/RNB2RK1 b - - 1 10","line":["Nxf2","Rxf2","Re1+","Bf1","Rxc1","Qxf7","Bxf2+","Qxf2","Qd4","a4","d5","a5"],"cp":9,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White spent five Knight moves grabbing a Rook in the corner while Black developed his whole army. An extra Rook is worth nothing if you get checkmated.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Qh4 5.Nb5 Bc5 6.Qf3 Nf6 7.Nxc7+ Kd8 8.Nxa8 Re8 9.Bd3 Nxe4 10.O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T27","q":"27","title":"Trap 27","page":29,"type":"play","fen":"r1b2rk1/pppp1p1p/2n2p2/2b5/3N3q/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1Q1RK1 w - - 2 11","line":["Nf5","Qf4","Qh5","Re8","Nh6+","Kg7","Qxf7+","Kxh6","Qxh7+","Kg5","h4+","Kg4"],"cp":748,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Queen went pawn hunting and ended up chased around with nowhere to hide. The opening is for developing pieces and keeping your King safe, not grabbing pawns with the Queen.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Bc5 5.c3 Nf6 6.Bg5 O-O 7.Bc4 Qe7 8.O-O Qxe4 9.Bxf6 gxf6 10.Bd3 Qh4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T28","q":"28","title":"Trap 28","page":30,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/pppp1ppp/2n2nq1/2b5/3NP3/2P1B3/PP2QPPP/RN2KB1R w KQkq - 3 8","line":["Nxc6","Bxe3","Ne5","Bxf2+","Kxf2","Qxe4","Kg1","Qxe2","Bxe2"],"cp":190,"need":3,"lesson":"Black answered a capture with his own in-between capture, but White had an even better in-between move that attacked the Queen. Before using a sneaky in-between move, check that your opponent doesn't have one too.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Bc5 5.Be3 Qf6 6.c3 Qg6 7.Qe2 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T29","q":"29","title":"Trap 29","page":31,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/2b5/3Nq3/2P1B3/PP2QPPP/RN2KB1R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["Nxc6"],"cp":314,"alt":["Nd2"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black moved his Queen three times just to grab a pawn, which was pure greed. In the opening, develop your pieces and castle instead of hunting pawns with your Queen.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Bc5 5.Be3 Qf6 6.c3 Qg6 7.Qe2 Qxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T30","q":"30","title":"Trap 30","page":32,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/ppppnppp/8/2b1q3/3n4/2P1B3/PP1N1PPP/R2QKB1R w KQkq - 0 9","line":["cxd4","Bxd4","Nc4","Bc3+","bxc3","Qxc3+","Nd2","Nd5","Rc1","Nxe3","Rxc3","Nxd1"],"cp":270,"need":1,"lesson":"Black happily grabbed the e5 pawn without asking why White let it go. It was a trap, so always look for the catch before taking free material.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Bc5 5.Be3 Qf6 6.c3 Nge7 7.Nd2 Nxd4 8.e5 Qxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T31","q":"31","title":"Trap 31","page":33,"type":"mate","fen":"r1b1k2r/ppp1qppp/5B2/3Pn3/8/8/PPP2PPP/RN1QKB1R b KQkq - 0 9","line":["Nf3#"],"mate":1,"need":1,"lesson":"White moved the same Knight over and over and left his King in the middle with the e-file open. Even a move that looks forced, like a recapture, should be checked for traps.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Bg5 Be7 6.Nf5 d5 7.exd5 Ne5 8.Nxe7 Qxe7 9.Bxf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T32","q":"32","title":"Trap 32","page":34,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/p1p2ppp/2p5/3pP3/1b3Pn1/2NB4/PPP3PP/R1BQ1RK1 b - f3 0 10","line":["Bc5+","Kh1","Qh4","Bxh7+","Kh8","Qxg4","Bxg4","Bd3","Bf2","a3","f6","e6"],"cp":880,"alt":["Qh4","Qh4"],"need":3,"lesson":"Pushing the f-pawn to protect e5 opened the diagonal to White's King and weakened g3. Be careful moving pawns in front of your castled King.","intro":"Scotch Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 Bb4 6.Nxc6 bxc6 7.Bd3 O-O 8.O-O d5 9.e5 Ng4 10.f4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Scotch Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T33","q":"33","title":"Trap 33","page":37,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/ppp2ppp/2n5/2bpp3/2BPP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq d6 0 5","line":["exd5","Nxd4"],"cp":331,"need":1,"lesson":"Black attacked too early and left his Knight unprotected on c4. White's Queen gave check and attacked the Knight at the same time.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Bc5 3.c3 Nc6 4.d4 d5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T34","q":"34","title":"Trap 34","page":38,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/ppp1bp1p/5np1/4Q3/2B2B2/2NP4/PPP3PP/R3K1NR w KQkq - 1 10","line":["Nd5","Nxd5","Qxh8+","Bf8","Ne2","Be6","O-O","Qe7","Rae1","Kd7","Nc3"],"cp":482,"need":3,"lesson":"Black played passive moves, gave up the center and had to retreat his Knight, wasting lots of time. Pushing the g-pawn then weakened his King's side and White crashed through.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d3 Be7 4.f4 exf4 5.e5 Ng8 6.Nc3 d6 7.Bxf4 dxe5 8.Qh5 g6 9.Qxe5 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T35","q":"35","title":"Trap 35","page":39,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1rk1/pp1pbppp/2p2n2/4N3/2B1P3/3P4/PPP1QPPP/RNB1K2R b KQ - 0 6","line":["Qa5+","Nd2","Qxe5","O-O","d5","Bb3","dxe4","Nxe4","Nxe4","Qxe4","Qxe4","dxe4"],"cp":341,"need":3,"lesson":"White grabbed the e5 pawn while his King was still in the middle and the diagonal to it was open. Black's Queen checked the King and attacked the Knight at once.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d3 c6 4.Qe2 Be7 5.Nf3 O-O 6.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T36","q":"36","title":"Trap 36","page":40,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1k2N/pp4pp/1qp2n2/2b1p3/4p3/1B1P4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQq - 0 8","line":["Bxf2+","Kf1","Bg4","Nc3","Bxd1","Nxd1","Bc5","Nf7","Nbd7","Nc3","e3","h3"],"cp":490,"need":5,"lesson":"White greedily grabbed a Rook instead of castling his King to safety. When your opponent leaves something hanging, ask yourself why before you take it.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d3 c6 4.Nf3 d5 5.Bb3 dxe4 6.Ng5 Bc5 7.Nxf7 Qb6 8.Nxh8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T37","q":"37","title":"Trap 37","page":41,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pppp1ppp/8/8/2nQ4/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 0 7","line":["Re1+","Qe7","Rxe7+","Bxe7","Qxc4","O-O","Qxc7","Nc6","Nc3","Nb4","Nd4"],"cp":741,"need":3,"lesson":"Black moved the same Knight four times in six moves and never developed his other pieces. Try to move a different piece each turn in the opening.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nf3 Nxe4 5.Qxd4 Nd6 6.O-O Nxc4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T38","q":"38","title":"Trap 38","page":42,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppppn1pp/3n1p2/8/3Q4/1B3N2/PPP2PPP/RNB1R1K1 w kq - 0 9","line":["Bf4","a5","Bxd6","cxd6","Nc3","a4","Bc4","Qa5","Nb5","d5","b4","Qa6"],"cp":770,"alt":["Qd5"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Knight on d6 blocked his own pawn, and his other pieces got stuck behind each other. Develop your pieces so they don't trip over one another.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nf3 Nxe4 5.Qxd4 Nd6 6.O-O Nc6 7.Re1+ Ne7 8.Bb3 f6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T39","q":"39","title":"Trap 39","page":43,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppppn2p/3n1p2/3Q2p1/8/1B3N2/PPP2PPP/RNB1R1K1 w kq g6 0 10","line":["Bf4","c6"],"cp":928,"alt":["Nxg5"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black's pieces were blocked in, pinned and tied down, and his King's pawns had moved forward. Develop quickly and in harmony, or your King will be left helpless.","intro":"Bishop's Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Bc4 Nf6 3.d4 exd4 4.Nf3 Nxe4 5.Qxd4 Nd6 6.O-O Nc6 7.Re1+ Ne7 8.Bb3 f6 9.Qd5 g5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Bishop's Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T40","q":"40","title":"Trap 40","page":44,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1qrk1/pppp1ppp/2n3n1/2b1p1BQ/2B1P3/2NP1N2/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 7 8","line":["Nd5","Bb6","Be3","Bxe3","fxe3","Qd8","Nc3","d5","Bxd5","Nb4","Ng5","h6"],"cp":287,"alt":["Be3"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black put his Knight on e7 instead of f6, so nothing guarded h5, and then moved the same Knight again. Bring out new pieces instead of moving ones that are already developed.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Bc5 3.Bc4 Ne7 4.d3 Nbc6 5.Qh5 O-O 6.Bg5 Qe8 7.Nf3 Ng6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T41","q":"41","title":"Trap 41","page":45,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkbnr/1pp2ppp/p2p4/4n3/2B1P1b1/2N2N2/PPPP2PP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["Nxe5","Qh4+"],"cp":444,"need":1,"lesson":"Black pinned the knight with his bishop too early and then recaptured with the wrong piece. The pinned knight could still jump away, because if Black grabbed the queen White would checkmate with Legal's Mate.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.f4 d6 4.Nf3 a6 5.Bc4 Bg4 6.fxe5 Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T42","q":"42","title":"Trap 42","page":46,"type":"mate","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2n5/2bp1P2/4n3/2N2N1P/PPPP2P1/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 1 8","line":["Qh4+","g3","Qxg3+","Ke2","Qf2+","Kd3","Nb4#"],"mate":4,"need":7,"lesson":"White wasted time with too many pawn moves like f5 and h3. Those moves left holes around his king, so he could not block a queen check on the e1-h4 diagonal.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.f4 Bc5 4.Nf3 d6 5.f5 Nf6 6.h3 d5 7.Nxe5 Nxe4 8.Nf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T43","q":"43","title":"Trap 43","page":47,"type":"mate","fen":"r1b1k1nr/pppp1ppp/2n5/2b5/2B1P2q/2N2Np1/PPPP3P/R1BQ1K1R b kq - 1 7","line":["g2+","Kxg2","Qf2+","Kh3","d5#"],"mate":3,"need":5,"lesson":"White let Black's queen check his king because he did not develop his knight to f3 in time to guard h4. Then pushing g3 opened his king up even more to Black's queen and bishop.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.f4 exf4 4.Bc4 Qh4+ 5.Kf1 Bc5 6.g3 fxg3 7.Nf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T44","q":"44","title":"Trap 44","page":48,"type":"play","fen":"r1b2k1r/pppp1ppp/1bn2n2/3Np3/2BqP1Q1/3P3N/PPP3PP/R1BK1R2 w - - 3 10","line":["Nxf6","d5","Nd7+","Ke8","Qxg7","Kxd7","Rxf7+","Kd6","c3","dxc4","cxd4","Nxd4"],"cp":897,"alt":["Rxf6"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black's queen went pawn-grabbing and ended up far from her own king. When your queen is off on an adventure, she can't help defend, so develop your pieces and keep your king safe first.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Qg4 Qf6 5.Nd5 Qxf2+ 6.Kd1 Kf8 7.Nh3 Qd4 8.d3 Bb6 9.Rf1 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T45","q":"45","title":"Trap 45","page":49,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P1Q1/2N2N2/PPPP1PPP/R1B1K2R b KQkq - 7 5","line":["d5","Qg3","dxc4","O-O","Nf6","Nxe5","Nd4","Nxc4","Be6","Qd3","Ng4","Rd1"],"cp":454,"need":3,"lesson":"White developed his knight without thinking and left his queen and bishop open to a discovered attack. Pushing d5 hits the bishop and opens the c8-bishop's line to the queen at the same time.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Qg4 Bf8 5.Nf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T46","q":"46","title":"Trap 46","page":50,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1rk1/ppp2ppp/3p4/2b1pP1Q/2B1P3/2NP1N2/PPP3PP/R1B1K2n w Q - 0 9","line":["Ng5","h6","Nxf7","Qe7","Nd8+","Kh7"],"cp":419,"need":3,"lesson":"Black moved the same knight four times just to grab a rook in the corner. That gave White lots of free moves to build a deadly attack on Black's king.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.d3 d6 5.f4 Ng4 6.f5 Nf2 7.Qh5 O-O 8.Nf3 Nxh1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T47","q":"47","title":"Trap 47","page":51,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1bkr/pppp2pp/2n5/4p3/4N3/5Q2/PPPP1PPP/R1B1K1NR w KQ - 3 7","line":["Ng5","Qf6","Qd5+","Qe6","Nxe6","dxe6","Qe4","Bd7","Nf3"],"cp":898,"need":5,"lesson":"After the fork trick, Black should have played d5 to grab the center and open a path for his bishop. Instead his king was left stuck on g8 where White's queen and knight could attack it.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.Bc4 Nxe4 4.Bxf7+ Kxf7 5.Nxe4 Nc6 6.Qf3+ Kg8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T48","q":"48","title":"Trap 48","page":52,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqnrk1/ppppbpp1/2n4p/4p1NQ/7P/1BNP4/PPP2PP1/R1B1K2R w KQ - 1 10","line":["Nxf7","Kh7","Ne4","Nd6","Nxd8","Nxd8","Ng5+","Kh8","Qg6","Bxg5","hxg5"],"cp":987,"need":5,"lesson":"Black castled right into the side where White was attacking, and then retreated his knight passively. Don't castle into a storm, and fight back instead of just waiting.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.Bc4 Nxe4 4.Qh5 Nd6 5.Bb3 Be7 6.d3 O-O 7.Nf3 Nc6 8.Ng5 h6 9.h4 Ne8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T49","q":"49","title":"Trap 49","page":53,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/ppppbpp1/2n2n1p/3Np1NQ/7P/1B1P4/PPP2PP1/R1B1K2R w KQ - 3 11","line":["Nxf6+","Bxf6","Nxf7","Rxf7","Qxf7+","Kh8","Bg5","d5","Bxd5","Bf5","Bxf6","Qxf6"],"cp":486,"alt":["Qg6"],"need":5,"lesson":"Black greedily took the queen without checking what would happen next, and got checkmated in two moves. Don't grab a sacrifice unless you have looked at your opponent's reply.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.Bc4 Nxe4 4.Qh5 Nd6 5.Bb3 Be7 6.d3 O-O 7.Nf3 Nc6 8.Ng5 h6 9.h4 Ne8 10.Nd5 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T50","q":"50","title":"Trap 50","page":54,"type":"play","fen":"rnkq1bnr/ppN2ppp/3Pb3/4N3/5p2/8/PPPPQ1PP/R1B1KB1R w KQ - 3 11","line":["Nxe6","Qh4+","Kd1","f3","Nxf3","Qh5","Nc7","Bxd6","Nxa8","Nf6","c3","Nc6"],"cp":1166,"need":1,"lesson":"Black gave up the center with exf4 and let White's pawn chase his knight away. Then his queen got pushed around and his king got stuck in the middle where White's pieces hunted it down.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.f4 exf4 4.e5 Qe7 5.Qe2 Ng8 6.Nf3 d6 7.Nd5 Qd8 8.exd6+ Be6 9.Nxc7+ Kd7 10.Ne5+ Kc8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T51","q":"51","title":"Trap 51","page":55,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppp1qppp/2np4/4P3/3P1p2/2N2N2/PPP1Q1PP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["Nd5","Nxd4","Nxd4","Bg4","exd6","Qxe2+","Bxe2","Bxe2","Nxc7+","Kd7","Nxa8","Bg4"],"cp":691,"need":3,"lesson":"Black gave up the center and put his queen on e7 where she blocked his bishop and could be chased. Opening the e-file with d6 let White's knight jump in and fork the king and rook.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.f4 exf4 4.e5 Qe7 5.Qe2 Ng8 6.Nf3 Nc6 7.d4 d6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T54","q":"54","title":"Trap 54","page":58,"type":"play","fen":"rnbk1b1r/ppp2ppp/8/3NP2q/8/3P1Nn1/PPP4P/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 1 9","line":["Nf4"],"cp":631,"need":1,"lesson":"Black's early queen check led him into trouble, and then he moved his king instead of grabbing the rook on h1. A lone queen surrounded by enemy bishops and knights can get trapped and lost.","intro":"Vienna Game. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nc3 Nf6 3.f4 d5 4.fxe5 Nxe4 5.d3 Qh4+ 6.g3 Nxg3 7.Nf3 Qh5 8.Nxd5 Kd8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Vienna Game","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T55","q":"55","title":"Trap 55","page":61,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kbnr/pppp1ppp/8/8/4Pp1q/5K2/PPPP2PP/RNBQ1BNR b kq - 3 4","line":["Qh5+","Kxf4","Bd6+","Ke3","Qxd1","Ne2","Nf6","Nbc3","Ng4+","Kd3","Nf2+","Ke3"],"cp":1535,"need":5,"lesson":"White walked his king out into the open for no good reason. Keep your king safe and get ready to castle instead of marching it up the board.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Kf2 Qh4+ 4.Kf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T56","q":"56","title":"Trap 56","page":62,"type":"mate","fen":"rnb1kbnr/pppp1ppp/8/8/4P2q/1P4pP/P1PP4/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5","line":["g2+","Ke2","Qxe4+","Kf2","gxh1=N#"],"mate":3,"need":5,"lesson":"White made pointless pawn moves instead of developing his pieces, which let Black's queen and pawn attack his king. Sometimes promoting to a knight is even better than making a new queen, because the knight gives check.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Promotion. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.b3 Qh4+ 4.g3 fxg3 5.h3. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Promotion"},{"id":"T57","q":"57","title":"Trap 57","page":63,"type":"playout","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp3p/5p2/6p1/2B1Pp1P/8/PPPP2P1/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 5","line":["Qh5+","Ke7","Qf7+","Kd6","e5+","Kc5","Qd5+","Kb6","Qb5#"],"mate":5,"goal":"mate","lesson":"Black made too many pawn moves and pushing the f-pawn opened a path for White's queen to his king. Develop your pieces instead of only moving pawns.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Bc4 g5 4.h4 f6. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T58","q":"58","title":"Trap 58","page":64,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1rk1/ppppnppp/1b6/6N1/2BPPB2/8/PPP3PP/RN1Q1K1R w - - 3 9","line":["Qh5","h6","Nxf7","d5","Nxd8","Rxf4+","Ke1","Rxe4+","Be2","Bg4","Qe8+","Kh7"],"cp":638,"need":5,"lesson":"Black castled right into White's attack while his queenside pieces were still sleeping at home. Don't castle into your opponent's attack, and fight back in the center first.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.d4 Qh4+ 5.Kf1 Bb6 6.Nf3 Qd8 7.Bxf4 Ne7 8.Ng5 O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T59","q":"59","title":"Trap 59","page":65,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq3r/ppppb1pp/8/8/3knpQ1/2N5/PPP3PP/R1B1K2R w KQ - 0 10","line":["Qxf4","Kc5"],"cp":305,"alt":["Be3+"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black brought his king forward to e6 when it could have hidden safely on g8. Extra pieces don't help you if your king is out in the open getting chased.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 Be7 4.Bc4 Nf6 5.Nc3 Nxe4 6.Bxf7+ Kxf7 7.Ne5+ Ke6 8.Qg4+ Kxe5 9.d4+ Kxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T60","q":"60","title":"Trap 60","page":66,"type":"mate","fen":"rn1qkbnr/ppp2ppp/8/8/4Np2/5b2/PPPPQ1PP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["Nf6#"],"mate":1,"need":1,"lesson":"Black brought out his bishop too early and forgot about the open e-file in front of his king. He should have blocked it by putting his queen or bishop on e7.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 d5 4.Nc3 dxe4 5.Nxe4 Bg4 6.Qe2 Bxf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T61","q":"61","title":"Trap 61","page":67,"type":"play","fen":"rn2kb1r/ppp2ppp/4B3/4N3/5p1q/2N3n1/PPPP2PP/R1BQ2KR b kq - 2 10","line":["Bc5+","d4","Bxd4+","Qxd4","Ne2+","Kf1","Nxd4","Bxf7+","Kf8","Bb3","Nbc6","Nd3"],"cp":745,"need":3,"lesson":"White never moved his d-pawn, so his queenside pieces could not come out to help. That left his king open on the a7-g1 diagonal, and Black's bishop and knight won the queen with a fork.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 Nf6 4.e5 Nh5 5.Nc3 d6 6.Bc4 dxe5 7.Nxe5 Qh4+ 8.Kf1 Be6 9.Bxe6 Ng3+ 10.Kg1. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T62","q":"62","title":"Trap 62","page":68,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq2nr/pppp1kbp/8/8/3PPB2/8/PPP3pP/RN1Q1RK1 w - - 0 9","line":["Qh5+","Ke7","Bd6+","Kxd6","Qd5+","Ke7","Qf7+","Kd6"],"cp":0,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black kept gobbling up pieces and pawns while his own army stayed at home. Grabbing material is no good if you never develop and your king gets left alone.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.Bc4 Bg7 5.d4 g4 6.Bxf4 gxf3 7.O-O fxg2 8.Bxf7+ Kxf7. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T63","q":"63","title":"Trap 63","page":69,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/ppppnp1p/8/8/2BPPb2/5Q2/PPP3PP/RN3RK1 w kq - 0 9","line":["Bxf7+","Kf8","Qxf4","Nf5","Qxf5","Qe7","Bh5+","Kg8","Rf3","Kg7","Qg4+","Kh6"],"cp":1151,"need":3,"lesson":"Black made five pawn moves and never moved his d-pawn to free his pieces. Bring out your center pawns and minor pieces quickly, or your king can get hunted down.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.Bc4 g4 5.d4 gxf3 6.Qxf3 Bh6 7.O-O Ne7 8.Bxf4 Bxf4. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T64","q":"64","title":"Trap 64","page":70,"type":"playout","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp3p/5p2/8/2B1PR2/2N5/PPPP2pP/R1BQ2K1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Qh5+","Ke7","Qf7+","Kd6","e5+","Kxe5","Re4+","Kd6","Qd5#"],"mate":5,"goal":"mate","lesson":"Black only moved pawns and grabbed pieces while all his pieces stayed on the back rank. Taking everything your opponent offers and never developing is a recipe for disaster.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.Bc4 g4 5.Nc3 gxf3 6.O-O fxg2 7.Rxf4 f6. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T65","q":"65","title":"Trap 65","page":71,"type":"mate","fen":"r1b1k1nr/ppppbp1p/n7/3NN3/3PP2Q/8/PPP4P/R1B1KB1q w Qkq - 1 11","line":["Qxe7+","Nxe7","Nf6+","Kf8","Bh6#"],"mate":3,"need":5,"lesson":"Black won a whole rook, but his new queen was stuck in the corner and his other pieces were not developed. Being ahead in material doesn't matter if your king gets checkmated.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.Nc3 g4 5.Ne5 Qh4+ 6.g3 fxg3 7.Qxg4 g2+ 8.Qxh4 gxh1=Q 9.Nd5 Na6 10.d4 Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T66","q":"66","title":"Trap 66","page":72,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1k2r/ppppbN1p/5n2/7Q/4P3/2N5/PPPP3P/R1B1KB1q w Qkq - 1 11","line":["Nd6+","Kd8","Nf7+","Ke8","Nd6+"],"cp":0,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black's tenth move was a mistake; checking with his bishop would have caused White real problems. Don't just make automatic moves when your king is in danger, look for active ideas.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.Nc3 g4 5.Ne5 Qh4+ 6.g3 fxg3 7.Qxg4 g2+ 8.Qxh4 gxh1=Q 9.Qh5 Be7 10.Nxf7 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T67","q":"67","title":"Trap 67","page":73,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/ppp2p1p/3b4/3P3n/2BP1pNP/8/PPP3P1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 9","line":["Ng3","Ne5"],"cp":508,"need":1,"lesson":"White grabbed the g4-pawn but left his pieces tangled up, with his rook stuck on h2 and his king on f2. When the diagonal to his king opened, his loose bishop on c4 got forked.","intro":"King's Gambit Accepted. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 exf4 3.Nf3 g5 4.h4 g4 5.Ne5 Nf6 6.Bc4 d5 7.exd5 Bd6 8.d4 Nh5 9.Nxg4. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Accepted","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T68","q":"68","title":"Trap 68","page":74,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kb1r/ppppqp2/n1n4p/4P1p1/2BP4/2N2N2/PPP3PP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq g6 0 10","line":["Nd5","Rh7","Nxe7","Bxe7","Be3","f6","exf6","Bxf6","c3","d6"],"cp":974,"need":3,"lesson":"Black wasted moves walking his knight to the edge of the board at a6 and weakened his king with h6 and g5. A knight on the rim is dim, and too many pawn moves near your king create holes.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Nf6 3.Nf3 Nc6 4.fxe5 Nxe4 5.d3 Nc5 6.d4 Na6 7.Bc4 Qe7 8.Nc3 h6 9.O-O g5. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T69","q":"69","title":"Trap 69","page":75,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk1nr/pppp1ppp/8/2b1P3/4P3/8/PPPP2PP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3","line":["Qh4+","g3","Qxe4+","Qe2","Qxh1","Nf3","Nc6","c3","Nge7","d4","Bb6","Na3"],"cp":561,"need":5,"lesson":"White grabbed a pawn while his king was still in the middle and e4 was unprotected. Black's queen checks on h4 and then forks the king and the rook.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Bc5 3.fxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T70","q":"70","title":"Trap 70","page":76,"type":"mate","fen":"r1b1k2r/pppp1ppp/2n2q2/2b1P3/4P3/2P3P1/PP1PN1Bn/RNBQKR2 b Qkq - 0 8","line":["Qxf1+","Bxf1","Nf3#"],"mate":2,"need":3,"lesson":"White's pieces were blocked in and his f3 square was weak. Capturing on e5 opened the f-file for Black's queen, who gave herself up to remove the guard so the knight could checkmate.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Bc5 3.Ne2 Qf6 4.c3 Nc6 5.g3 Nh6 6.Bg2 Ng4 7.Rf1 Nxh2 8.fxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T71","q":"71","title":"Trap 71","page":77,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2N/ppp1q1pp/5n2/2b5/3npP2/2N5/PPPP2PP/R1BQKB1R b KQq - 2 9","line":["Nf3+","Ke2","Bg4","b4","Nxh2+","Ke1","Nf3+","gxf3","exf3+","Qe2","fxe2","Bxe2"],"cp":792,"need":3,"lesson":"White's knight went off to grab the rook in the corner, where it was stuck and useless. Meanwhile Black's pieces were all developed and ready to attack White's king.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Bc5 3.Nf3 d5 4.Nxe5 dxe4 5.Nc3 Nf6 6.Qe2 Nc6 7.Nxf7 Qe7 8.Nxh8 Nd4 9.Qd1. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T72","q":"72","title":"Trap 72","page":78,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk1nr/ppp1bppp/8/n3p3/2B1P1b1/2P2N2/PP1P2PP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Bxf7+","Kf8"],"cp":658,"need":1,"lesson":"Black moved his knight to the edge at a5, where it no longer protected e5 or helped guard the bishop. That let White sacrifice on f7 and then fork the king and bishop with his knight.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d6 3.Nf3 Bg4 4.Bc4 Be7 5.O-O Nc6 6.c3 Na5 7.fxe5 dxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T73","q":"73","title":"Trap 73","page":79,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/ppp2ppp/2n5/3P4/1b2pP2/2N2N2/PP4PP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 8","line":["exf3","Qxf3","Qe7+","Qe3","Nd4","Bd3","Bf5","Kf2","Bxd3","Qxd3","Nf6"],"cp":600,"need":1,"lesson":"Both sides had pieces attacked by pawns, but Black got to move first. By capturing the knight and then removing the guard with Bxc3+, Black wins White's queen or rook.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Bc5 3.Nf3 Nc6 4.c3 d5 5.d4 exd4 6.cxd4 Bb4+ 7.Nc3 dxe4 8.d5. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T74","q":"74","title":"Trap 74","page":80,"type":"play","fen":"r2q2nr/ppp2kpp/2np4/2b1p1N1/4PPb1/2P5/PP1P2PP/RNBQK2R b KQ - 1 7","line":["Qxg5","Qb3+","Be6","fxg5","Bxb3","axb3","Nge7","b4","Bb6","b5","Nd8","Rf1+"],"cp":473,"need":1,"lesson":"White gave up his Bishop for a flashy check, but Black could give back his Queen for the Knight and then take White's Queen. Before starting a combination, check whether your opponent has a counter-trick of his own.","intro":"King's Gambit Declined. Theme: Desperado. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 Bc5 3.Nf3 Nc6 4.Bc4 d6 5.c3 Bg4 6.Bxf7+ Kxf7 7.Ng5+. Now find the zap!","opening":"King's Gambit Declined","tactic":"Desperado"},{"id":"T75","q":"75","title":"Trap 75","page":81,"type":"play","fen":"B2qkb1r/p1pb1ppp/5n2/8/4pP2/8/PPPP2PP/RNBQK2R b KQk - 0 8","line":["Qxa8","O-O"],"cp":-97,"alt":["Bg4"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White grabbed the Rook in the corner, but that left his Queen stuck and attacked with no good escape. Grabbing material while your pieces are undeveloped can cost you your Queen.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.Nf3 dxe4 4.Nxe5 Nc6 5.Bb5 Nf6 6.Nxc6 bxc6 7.Bxc6+ Bd7 8.Bxa8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T76","q":"76","title":"Trap 76","page":82,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqkbnr/ppp2ppp/8/3Np3/3pPP2/8/PPPP2PP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 4","line":["c6","Qh5"],"cp":328,"need":1,"lesson":"White sent his Knight deep into enemy territory where it had no safe square to run back to. One pawn push trapped it and won it.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.Nc3 d4 4.Nd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T77","q":"77","title":"Trap 77","page":83,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1k1nr/ppp2ppp/3bq3/8/5p2/2N2N2/PPPP1KPP/R1BQ1B1R w kq - 2 7","line":["Bb5+"],"cp":615,"need":1,"lesson":"Black brought his Queen out early and left it on the same line as his King. A Rook on that open file pinned the Queen and won it.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.exd5 Qxd5 4.Nc3 Qe6 5.Nf3 exf4+ 6.Kf2 Bd6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T78","q":"78","title":"Trap 78","page":84,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk1nr/pp2bpQp/2p5/8/5P2/2N5/PPPP2PP/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 0 7","line":["Bf6","Qxh8","Bxh8","Be2","Nd7","g3","Nc5","Nf3","Bf5"],"cp":570,"need":3,"lesson":"White's Queen went pawn-hunting deep in Black's camp and got trapped and pinned against her own King. Beware of 'poisoned pawns' that lure your Queen away.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.exd5 Qxd5 4.Nc3 Qd8 5.Qe2 c6 6.Qxe5+ Be7 7.Qxg7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T79","q":"79","title":"Trap 79","page":85,"type":"play","fen":"rn2kb1r/ppp2ppp/8/3P1b2/4nP1q/3P2P1/PPP1Q2P/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 0 8","line":["Qe7","Nf3","Nd6","Be3","Nd7","O-O-O","O-O-O","Bxa7","Qxe2","Bxe2","Nf6","Nd2"],"cp":205,"need":3,"lesson":"White blocked the check with a pawn move that weakened the long diagonal to his Rook in the corner. Black unpinned his Knight, and White ended up pinned himself and lost material.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.exd5 e4 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.Qe2 Bf5 6.Nxe4 Nxe4 7.d3 Qh4+ 8.g3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T80","q":"80","title":"Trap 80","page":86,"type":"play","fen":"rn2kbnr/p4ppp/2pq4/8/B3pPb1/2P5/PP1PN1PP/RNBQ1RK1 b kq - 4 9","line":["Nf6","Kh1"],"cp":15,"alt":["Nd7"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White looked developed, but his Queenside pieces never moved and his Knight was pinned. Black's Queen and Bishops swarmed the weak King for a mating attack.","intro":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.f4 d5 3.exd5 e4 4.Bb5+ c6 5.dxc6 bxc6 6.Ba4 Qd4 7.c3 Qd6 8.Ne2 Bg4 9.O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"Falkbeer Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T81","q":"81","title":"Trap 81","page":91,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kbnr/ppppq1pp/5p2/4N2Q/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1KB1R b KQkq - 2 4","line":["g6","Nxg6"],"cp":256,"need":1,"lesson":"White brought his Queen out too early. After the Knight jumped to g6, Black's Queen gave check while attacking the Knight and won it.","intro":"Damiano Defense. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 f6 3.Nxe5 Qe7 4.Qh5+. Now find the zap!","opening":"Damiano Defense","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T82","q":"82","title":"Trap 82","page":92,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1bnr/ppp3p1/6kp/3BQ3/4P2P/8/PPPP1PP1/RNB1K2R w KQ - 0 9","line":["Bxb7","Ne7","Qg3+","Kh7","Bxa8","Nbc6","Qc3","Nd4","b3","Ba6","d3"],"cp":620,"need":5,"lesson":"Black's f-pawn move opened lines to his King and let White hunt it down. Black's Bishop had too many jobs, so White could grab pawns and stay way ahead.","intro":"Damiano Defense. Theme: Overload. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 f6 3.Nxe5 fxe5 4.Qh5+ Ke7 5.Qxe5+ Kf7 6.Bc4+ d5 7.Bxd5+ Kg6 8.h4 h6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Damiano Defense","tactic":"Overload"},{"id":"T83","q":"83","title":"Trap 83","page":93,"type":"play","fen":"rnbq1bnr/ppp3pp/6k1/3BQ3/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQ d3 0 8","line":["Bd6","Qg5+","Qxg5","Bxg5","Kxg5","e5","Bf8","h4+","Kh6","Nd2","Ne7","Be4"],"cp":352,"need":5,"lesson":"White's pawn move looked natural, but it left his Queen in the middle with no escape. He had to give up a piece to save her, and three pawns are not enough for a Knight and a Bishop.","intro":"Damiano Defense. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 f6 3.Nxe5 fxe5 4.Qh5+ Ke7 5.Qxe5+ Kf7 6.Bc4+ d5 7.Bxd5+ Kg6 8.d4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Damiano Defense","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T86","q":"86","title":"Trap 86","page":96,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kbnr/ppp3pp/3p2q1/8/2NPp3/8/PPP1BPPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 2 7","line":["Bh5","Bf5","Bxg6+","Bxg6","Nc3","Nd7","h3","O-O-O","Ne3","Ngf6","O-O","Kb8"],"cp":854,"need":3,"lesson":"Black put his Queen on the same diagonal as his King, which his early f-pawn move had opened up. A Bishop slid to h5 and pinned the Queen.","intro":"Latvian Counter-Gambit. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 f5 3.Nxe5 Qf6 4.d4 d6 5.Nc4 fxe4 6.Be2 Qg6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Latvian Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T87","q":"87","title":"Trap 87","page":97,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqkbnr/ppp3pp/8/4Np2/4B3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","line":["Qd4","f4","Qxe4+","Qe2","Qxe2+","Kxe2","Nf6","Re1","Nc6","Nxc6","bxc6","Nc3"],"cp":414,"need":3,"lesson":"White put his Bishop on d3 where it blocked his pawns, then let it and his Knight get attacked together. Black's Queen attacked both pieces at once and won one.","intro":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d5 3.Bd3 dxe4 4.Bxe4 f5 5.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T88","q":"88","title":"Trap 88","page":98,"type":"play","fen":"rn3bnr/ppp1k1pp/8/4N3/2BPp3/7b/PPP2P1q/RNBQKR2 w Q - 0 9","line":["Bg5+","Nf6"],"cp":801,"alt":["Qh5","Qh5"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black got greedy and kept grabbing pawns with his Queen instead of developing. White pinned and hunted the Queen, and Black had to give up his Bishop to save her.","intro":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d5 3.Nxe5 dxe4 4.Bc4 Qg5 5.Bxf7+ Ke7 6.d4 Qxg2 7.Rf1 Bh3 8.Bc4 Qxh2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T89","q":"89","title":"Trap 89","page":99,"type":"play","fen":"rn3b1r/ppp1kNpp/5n2/8/2BPp3/7b/PPP2PqP/RNBQKR2 b Q - 5 9","line":["b5","Nxh8"],"cp":210,"need":1,"lesson":"White's Knight went after the Rook in the corner, but his Bishop was guarding too many things. Black chased the Bishop away and won a piece, and the greedy Knight got trapped.","intro":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit. Theme: Overload. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d5 3.Nxe5 dxe4 4.Bc4 Qg5 5.Bxf7+ Ke7 6.d4 Qxg2 7.Rf1 Bh3 8.Bc4 Nf6 9.Nf7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Overload"},{"id":"T90","q":"90","title":"Trap 90","page":100,"type":"play","fen":"rnb2Q2/ppp3pp/8/4k3/4p3/8/PPPPKP1P/RNB4q b - - 0 11","line":["Bg4+","f3","Bxf3+","Qxf3","Qxf3+","Ke1","Qh1+","Kf2","Qxh2+","Ke3","Qg1+","Ke2"],"cp":1629,"need":5,"lesson":"White kept grabbing pieces with his Queen instead of bringing out his other pieces. Black's Bishop and Queen then teamed up against White's lonely King.","intro":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d5 3.Nxe5 dxe4 4.Bc4 Qg5 5.Bxf7+ Ke7 6.Qh5 Qxg2 7.Bxg8 Qxh1+ 8.Ke2 Rxg8 9.Qf7+ Kd6 10.Qxg8 Kxe5 11.Qxf8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Queen's Pawn Counter-Gambit","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T91","q":"91","title":"Trap 91","page":101,"type":"play","fen":"r3kbnr/ppp2ppp/8/q2Ppb2/1n6/2N5/PPPBNPPP/2RQKB1R b Kkq - 4 8","line":["Bxc2","Qxc2","Nxc2+","Rxc2","O-O-O","Ng3","Bb4","Bc4","Bxc3","Bxc3","Qc5"],"cp":558,"need":3,"lesson":"White guarded c2 with his Rook, but his own pieces boxed in his King. Black removed the guard and the Knight gave a smothered mate.","intro":"Alapin Opening. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Ne2 d5 3.exd5 Qxd5 4.Nbc3 Qa5 5.d4 Nc6 6.d5 Nb4 7.Bd2 Bf5 8.Rc1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Alapin Opening","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T92","q":"92","title":"Trap 92","page":102,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/pppp1ppp/1b6/4n3/3Pn2q/2P3P1/PP1NN2P/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 9","line":["Qc2","Qg4","Qxe4","Qxe4","Nxe4","Nd3+","Kd2","Nxc1","Rxc1","O-O","Nf4","Re8"],"cp":360,"need":5,"lesson":"Black threw all his pieces at White's King, but they were hanging and unprotected. White blocked the main threat and then won a loose piece.","intro":"Alapin Opening. Theme: Multiple Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Ne2 Bc5 3.c3 Nc6 4.d4 Bb6 5.f4 Nf6 6.fxe5 Nxe4 7.Nd2 Qh4+ 8.g3 Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Alapin Opening","tactic":"Multiple Attack"},{"id":"T93","q":"93","title":"Trap 93","page":103,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppppb2p/2n3p1/3N1p2/2Bp2Q1/6P1/PPP2PP1/R1B1K2R w KQkq f6 0 10","line":["Qe2","h5","Bg5","Kf8","Nxe7","Nxe7","O-O-O","Rh7","Rxd4","b5","Bb3","a5"],"cp":490,"alt":["Rxh7"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black was ahead in pawns but pushed his f-pawn and weakened his King. White gave up his Queen and his pieces swarmed in for checkmate.","intro":"Alapin Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Ne2 Nf6 3.d4 Nxe4 4.Ng3 Nxg3 5.hxg3 Nc6 6.Nc3 exd4 7.Nd5 Be7 8.Qg4 g6 9.Bc4 f5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Alapin Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T94","q":"94","title":"Trap 94","page":104,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/pppp1ppp/5n2/2b1p1B1/4P3/3P4/PPP1NPPP/RN1QKB1R b KQkq - 2 4","line":["Bxf2+","Kxf2","Ng4+","Kg1","Qxg5","Qd2","Qf6","Nec3","Qb6+","d4","Qxb2"],"cp":392,"need":3,"lesson":"White pinned the Knight without thinking about his weak f2 square. The Knight jumped away anyway, and if White took the Queen, Black gave checkmate.","intro":"Alapin Opening. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Ne2 Nf6 3.d3 Bc5 4.Bg5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Alapin Opening","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T95","q":"95","title":"Trap 95","page":105,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kb1r/pp1p1ppp/2p5/3Nq3/4n3/2N5/PPPPQ1PP/R1B1KB1R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["d4","Qf5","Nxe4","Kd8","Ndc3","d5","Ng3","Qe6","Qxe6","Bxe6","Bd3","Nd7"],"cp":424,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Queen was trying to do everything by herself while the other pieces stayed home. White pushed a pawn to knock her off guard duty and won material.","intro":"Alapin Opening. Theme: Overload. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Ne2 Nf6 3.f4 exf4 4.Nxf4 Nxe4 5.Qe2 Qe7 6.Nd5 Qe5 7.Nbc3 c6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Alapin Opening","tactic":"Overload"},{"id":"T96","q":"96","title":"Trap 96","page":106,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/p1p2ppp/2pb4/3p4/Q3P1n1/2PP4/PP2BPPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 3 9","line":["Qxc6","Be6","Bxg4","Bxg4","h3","dxe4","hxg4","exd3","Qf3"],"cp":267,"need":3,"lesson":"Black moved his Knight to attack, but forgot that White's Queen could reach his Bishop along the 4th rank. One pawn push attacked two Bishops at once.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 d5 4.Qa4 Nf6 5.Nxe5 Bd6 6.Nxc6 bxc6 7.d3 O-O 8.Be2 Ng4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T97","q":"97","title":"Trap 97","page":107,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppp2ppp/2n5/1B2q3/Q3p3/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["Bxc6+"],"cp":157,"need":1,"lesson":"Black's Knight was pinned to his King, and he grabbed a piece without fixing the pin. White took the Knight with check and then won Black's pawn and a safe position.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 d5 4.Qa4 dxe4 5.Nxe5 Qd5 6.Bb5 Qxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T98","q":"98","title":"Trap 98","page":108,"type":"mate","fen":"r6r/pppk1ppp/2n5/1Bbq1n2/Q3pP2/1PP5/P2P2PP/RNB2R1K b - - 2 11","line":["Ng3+","hxg3","Qh5#"],"mate":2,"need":3,"lesson":"White's Queen wandered off to a4 and his Queenside pieces never moved, so nobody was left to defend his King. Black's well-placed pieces finished with checkmate.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 d5 4.Qa4 dxe4 5.Nxe5 Qd5 6.Bb5 Ne7 7.f4 Bd7 8.Nxd7 Kxd7 9.O-O Nf5 10.b3 Bc5+ 11.Kh1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T99","q":"99","title":"Trap 99","page":109,"type":"mate","fen":"r3kb1r/pQpbqppp/8/1B6/3Pn3/2P2n2/PP3PPP/RNB2K1R b kq - 2 10","line":["Ng3+","hxg3","Qe1#"],"mate":2,"need":3,"lesson":"White's Queen went far away to grab pawns and could not help defend her King. Black's pieces jumped in and gave checkmate.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 Nf6 4.d4 d5 5.Bb5 Nxe4 6.Nxe5 Bd7 7.Qb3 Qe7 8.Qxd5 Nxe5 9.Qxb7 Nf3+ 10.Kf1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T100","q":"100","title":"Trap 100","page":110,"type":"play","fen":"rnb1kb1r/pppp1ppp/4n3/3qN1B1/8/2PB4/PP3PPP/RN1QR1K1 w kq - 2 11","line":["Bg6","Qxe5","Bxf7+","Kxf7","Rxe5","Nc6","Rf5+","Kg8","Be3","d6","Nd2","g6"],"cp":625,"need":5,"lesson":"Black kept moving his Queen and Knight while his other pieces stayed home. A Bishop move uncovered an attack on the Queen and threatened checkmate at the same time.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 Nf6 4.d4 Nxe4 5.d5 Nb8 6.Bd3 Nc5 7.Nxe5 Qe7 8.O-O Qd6 9.Bg5 Qxd5 10.Re1 Ne6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T101","q":"101","title":"Trap 101","page":111,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/6n1/3PN3/8/2PB4/PP3nPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["Bxg6","hxg6","Kxf2","Qh4+","Kf1","Rh5","Nf3","Qe4","Qe2","Qxe2+","Kxe2","Rxd5"],"cp":213,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's lone Knight charged in to grab the Queen while White's pieces were ready to attack. White gave up the Queen and chased Black's King into a checkmate.","intro":"Ponziani Opening. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.c3 Nf6 4.d4 Nxe4 5.d5 Ne7 6.Nxe5 Ng6 7.Bd3 Nxf2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ponziani Opening","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T102","q":"102","title":"Trap 102","page":115,"type":"play","fen":"rn1qkbnr/ppp2pp1/3p3p/4p3/2B1P1b1/2N2N2/PPPP1PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","line":["Nxe5","dxe5","Qxg4","Nf6","Qg3","Qe7","O-O","Nc6","d3","Nd4"],"cp":204,"alt":["h3"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black pinned White's knight with the bishop but then wasted a move with h6. The pin was not real, and White's knights and bishop teamed up for Legal's Mate.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.Bc4 Bg4 4.Nc3 h6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T103","q":"103","title":"Trap 103","page":116,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkbnr/ppp2ppp/2np4/4p2b/2B1P3/2N2N1P/PPPP1PP1/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 1 6","line":["O-O","Nf6"],"cp":141,"alt":["d3"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black brought the bishop out too early and then backed it up to h5, where nothing protected it. White broke the pin, won the bishop, and came out a pawn ahead with a forking queen check.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.Bc4 Bg4 4.Nc3 Nc6 5.h3 Bh5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T104","q":"104","title":"Trap 104","page":117,"type":"playout","fen":"r2qkb1r/pppb2pp/2np1n2/5pN1/2BQP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 3 8","line":["Bf7+","Ke7","Qxf6+","Kxf6","Nd5+","Ke5","Nf3+","Kxe4","Nc3#"],"mate":5,"goal":"mate","lesson":"Pushing the f-pawn opened lines toward Black's king, and Black wasted time chasing White's queen instead of protecting f7. White sacrificed the queen and the knights chased the king to its doom.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.Bc4 f5 4.d4 Nf6 5.Nc3 exd4 6.Qxd4 Bd7 7.Ng5 Nc6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T105","q":"105","title":"Trap 105","page":118,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/pppnbppp/3p4/8/2BNP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 6","line":["O-O","Ngf6","Nc3","O-O","Bd2","Kh8","h3","Ne5","Bb3","c6","Nf5","Bxf5"],"cp":103,"alt":["f4","Bxf7+"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black's knight on d7 blocked the bishop and left the e6 square weak. White sacrificed on f7, jumped a knight into e6, and drew Black's king out into a mating net.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.Bc4 Be7 4.d4 exd4 5.Nxd4 Nd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T106","q":"106","title":"Trap 106","page":119,"type":"mate","fen":"r1bqk2r/pp1nb2p/2ppp2p/4p3/2BPP3/8/PPP2PPP/RN1Q1RK1 w kq - 0 9","line":["Qh5+","Kf8","Bxe6","exd4","Qf7#"],"mate":3,"need":5,"lesson":"Black's bishop on e7 jammed up Black's own pieces so they could not defend. After White's sacrifices ripped away the f- and g-pawns, the king had no shelter left.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 Nd7 4.Bc4 c6 5.Ng5 Nh6 6.O-O Be7 7.Ne6 fxe6 8.Bxh6 gxh6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T107","q":"107","title":"Trap 107","page":120,"type":"play","fen":"rn1qkb1r/ppp2ppp/5n2/4p3/2B1P3/5Q2/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 2 7","line":["Qb3","Qe7"],"cp":175,"alt":["O-O"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black traded away the light-square bishop early, leaving f7 and b7 weak. White's queen forked both pawns and won material.","intro":"Philidor Defense. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 Bg4 4.dxe5 Bxf3 5.Qxf3 dxe5 6.Bc4 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Philidor Defense","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T108","q":"108","title":"Trap 108","page":121,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pppp1ppp/5n2/4N3/8/8/PPPPQPPP/RNB1KB1R w KQkq - 2 5","line":["Nc6+","Be7","Nxd8","Kxd8","c3","Nc6","d3","d6","Nd2","Bd7","Nc4","Kc8"],"cp":866,"need":3,"lesson":"Black copied White's moves and then retreated the knight, opening the e-file to Black's king. White's knight jumped away with a discovered check from the queen and then captured Black's queen.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Nxe5 Nxe4 4.Qe2 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T109","q":"109","title":"Trap 109","page":122,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2p2n2/2b3B1/4P3/3P4/PPP2PPP/RN1QKB1R b KQkq - 2 6","line":["Nxe4","Be3","Bxe3","fxe3","Qh4+","g3","Nxg3","hxg3","Qxh1"],"cp":507,"need":3,"lesson":"White brought out the queen's bishop too early to pin a knight, but the pin was fake. Black jumped the knight anyway, and taking Black's queen led straight to mate.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Nxe5 Nc6 4.Nxc6 dxc6 5.d3 Bc5 6.Bg5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T110","q":"110","title":"Trap 110","page":123,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2p5/2b1P3/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 7","line":["Bxf2+","Kxf2","Qxd1","Nc3","Qxc2+","Be2","Be6","Rf1","h6","Kg1","Rd8","Kh1"],"cp":642,"need":3,"lesson":"White grabbed the knight while having no pieces developed, so the king had to guard both the queen and f2. A bishop check on f2 pulled the king away and Black won White's queen.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Nxe5 Nc6 4.Nxc6 dxc6 5.e5 Ne4 6.d3 Bc5 7.dxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T111","q":"111","title":"Trap 111","page":124,"type":"play","fen":"rn2kb1r/pp2qppp/2pp4/7Q/3Pn3/5N1P/PPP2PP1/RNB1KB1R b KQkq - 0 9","line":["Nf6+","Kd1","Nxh5","Bd3","Qd8","a3","Qb6","Nbd2","d5","a4","Nd7","a5"],"cp":831,"need":3,"lesson":"White's queen went on a greedy hunt while Black's queen stared down the open e-file at White's king. Black's knight moved with a discovered check and then gobbled the White queen.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Nxe5 d6 4.Nf3 Nxe4 5.d4 Bg4 6.h3 Bh5 7.Qd3 Qe7 8.Qb5+ c6 9.Qxh5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T112","q":"112","title":"Trap 112","page":125,"type":"play","fen":"rn1qkb1r/ppp2ppp/3p4/4p3/2B3b1/2P2N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 2 7","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Nxe5+","Ke8","Nxg4","h5","Re1+","Be7","Ne3","Bf6","Qf3","Nd7"],"cp":442,"alt":["Nxe5"],"need":5,"lesson":"Black grabbed a pawn and then pinned a knight instead of developing and castling. The pin did not hold, and taking White's queen allowed a quick mate.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.Bc4 Nxe4 4.Nc3 Nxc3 5.dxc3 d6 6.O-O Bg4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T113","q":"113","title":"Trap 113","page":126,"type":"play","fen":"rn2kb1r/ppp1qppp/8/8/3Q4/2N1BN2/PPb2PPP/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 11","line":["Nd5","Nc6","Qf4","Qd6","Nxc7+","Kd7","Qxd6+","Bxd6","Nxa8","Rxa8","O-O","Bg6"],"cp":205,"alt":["Qd2"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black moved the same knight four times and then went pawn-hunting while far behind in development. White developed with threats, and the knight fork on c7 won Black's rook.","intro":"Petroff Defense. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nf6 3.d4 exd4 4.e5 Ne4 5.Qxd4 d5 6.exd6 Nxd6 7.Bd3 Qe7+ 8.Be3 Nf5 9.Bxf5 Bxf5 10.Nc3 Bxc2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Petroff Defense","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T114","q":"114","title":"Trap 114","page":127,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k1nr/pppp1ppp/5q2/3Nn3/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 2 7","line":["Nf3+","gxf3","Qxd4","Nxc7+","Kf8","Nxa8","Qe5","Bd3","Qb8","e5","Qxa8","O-O"],"cp":348,"need":3,"lesson":"White went for a knight fork but forgot that the queen on d4 was unprotected. Black's knight gave a check that uncovered an attack on White's queen.","intro":"Three Knights Game. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Bc5 4.Nxe5 Nxe5 5.d4 Bxd4 6.Qxd4 Qf6 7.Nd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Three Knights Game","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T115","q":"115","title":"Trap 115","page":128,"type":"play","fen":"r1bk2nr/pppp1ppp/5q2/1N2n3/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R w KQ - 3 8","line":["Qc5","d5","Qxc7+","Ke8","Nd6+","Kf8","Nxc8","Qc6","Qd8+","Qe8","Qxe8+","Kxe8"],"cp":769,"need":3,"lesson":"Black had to move the king just to guard c7, which shows how much trouble Black was in. White's queen then threatened two different mates at once.","intro":"Three Knights Game. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Bc5 4.Nxe5 Nxe5 5.d4 Bxd4 6.Qxd4 Qf6 7.Nb5 Kd8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Three Knights Game","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T116","q":"116","title":"Trap 116","page":129,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp4p/2n2nN1/7Q/2BPp3/8/PPP2PPP/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 1 10","line":["Bf7+","Kd7","Qh3+","Ng4","Qxg4+","Kd6","Qxe4","Qg5","Bf4+","Qe5","dxe5+","Kc5"],"cp":2265,"need":5,"lesson":"Pushing the f-pawn early weakened the diagonal to Black's king. When Black's knight left f6, White's queen and bishops poured in with checks.","intro":"Three Knights Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 f5 4.d4 fxe4 5.Nxe5 Nf6 6.Bc4 d5 7.Nxd5 Nxd5 8.Qh5+ g6 9.Nxg6 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Three Knights Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T117","q":"117","title":"Trap 117","page":130,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/ppp1nppp/3p1n2/2bNp3/2B1P1b1/2PP1N2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 1 9","line":["Nxe5","Nexd5","Nxg4","Nb6","Bb3","Nbd7","d4","Bb6","e5","dxe5","dxe5","Nxg4"],"cp":405,"alt":["Nxf6+"],"need":3,"lesson":"Moving the knight from c6 to e7 weakened e5 and let White break the pin. If Black takes the queen, White's knight and bishops give mate.","intro":"Four Knights Game. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Bc4 Bb4 5.O-O d6 6.Nd5 Bg4 7.c3 Bc5 8.d3 Ne7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Four Knights Game","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T118","q":"118","title":"Trap 118","page":131,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppppbppp/8/1B6/8/2P5/PPP2PPP/R1BQR1K1 w kq - 2 11","line":["Bg5","f6","Bxf6","gxf6","Qh5+","Kf8","Bc4","d5"],"cp":531,"need":3,"lesson":"Black blocked the check with the bishop and left the king stuck in the center with no pieces developed. White's attack against f7 came too fast to stop.","intro":"Four Knights Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Bb5 Bb4 5.O-O Nd4 6.Nxd4 exd4 7.e5 dxc3 8.dxc3 Be7 9.exf6 Bxf6 10.Re1+ Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Four Knights Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T119","q":"119","title":"Trap 119","page":132,"type":"play","fen":"r4rk1/pppq1ppp/3p1n2/4p1B1/1NBnP1b1/3P1N2/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 10","line":["Bxf3","gxf3","Qh3","Bxf6","Nxf3+","Qxf3","Qxf3","Be7","Rfe8","Bh4","c6","Bg3"],"cp":417,"need":3,"lesson":"White greedily grabbed the bishop and missed why Black played Qd7. Black traded on f3 to wreck White's king cover, and the queen jumped to h3 to threaten mate.","intro":"Four Knights Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Bb5 Bb4 5.O-O O-O 6.d3 d6 7.Bg5 Bg4 8.Nd5 Nd4 9.Bc4 Qd7 10.Nxb4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Four Knights Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T120","q":"120","title":"Trap 120","page":133,"type":"play","fen":"r4rk1/pppq1ppp/3p1n2/3Np1B1/3nP1b1/3P1N2/PPPQ1PPP/R4RK1 w - - 4 12","line":["Nxf6+","gxf6","Bxf6","Ne2+","Qxe2","Qe6","Bh4","c6","Kh1","Kg7","Rg1","f6"],"cp":579,"alt":["Bxf6"],"need":5,"lesson":"Black just copied White's moves, but copying does not work forever. White broke the symmetry first and crashed through to Black's king.","intro":"Four Knights Game. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Bb5 Bb4 5.O-O O-O 6.d3 d6 7.Bg5 Bg4 8.Nd5 Nd4 9.Nxb4 Nxb5 10.Nd5 Nd4 11.Qd2 Qd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Four Knights Game","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T121","q":"121","title":"Trap 121","page":137,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pp1pbppp/5n2/2p1P3/2BQ4/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq c6 0 8","line":["Qd1","d5","exf6","dxc4","fxe7","Qxd1+","Kxd1","Kxe7","Re1+","Be6","Nc3","Rad8+"],"cp":383,"alt":["Qf4"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black traded knights, which helped White's queen get to the center, and then attacked it without a real plan. White's queen moved to f4, pinning the knight that guarded f7.","intro":"Hungarian Defense. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Be7 4.d4 exd4 5.Nxd4 Nxd4 6.Qxd4 Nf6 7.e5 c5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Hungarian Defense","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T122","q":"122","title":"Trap 122","page":138,"type":"mate","fen":"r1bqk1nr/ppp1bppp/2np4/3Q4/2B1P3/2p2N2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["Qxf7+","Kd7","Be6#"],"mate":2,"need":3,"lesson":"Black greedily grabbed another pawn and let White's queen reach d5 to team up with the bishop against f7. Only the king guarded f7, so it fell with mate right away.","intro":"Hungarian Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Be7 4.d4 exd4 5.c3 dxc3 6.Qd5 d6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Hungarian Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T123","q":"123","title":"Trap 123","page":139,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqr1k1/pppnbppp/2np4/8/2BNP3/2N4P/PPP2PP1/R1BQR1K1 w - - 3 10","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Ne6","Nf6","Nxd8+","Bxd8","Be3","Bd7","f3","Kg8","a4","h6"],"cp":630,"need":5,"lesson":"Black's knight on d7 boxed in Black's own bishop and queen and left the king without helpers. White sacrificed on f7 and e6 to drag the king out for mate.","intro":"Hungarian Defense. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Be7 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.d4 exd4 6.Nxd4 d6 7.O-O O-O 8.h3 Re8 9.Re1 Nd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Hungarian Defense","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T124","q":"124","title":"Trap 124","page":140,"type":"mate","fen":"r1bq1b1r/pppknBp1/2np4/4pPNp/6Q1/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB2RK1 w - h6 0 9","line":["f6+","hxg4","Be6+","Ke8","f7#"],"mate":3,"need":5,"lesson":"Black's knight on e7 left f7 weak, and then Black weakened the king even more with f6. Attacking White's queen with h5 did not help, because White gave up the queen for a pawn mate.","intro":"Paris Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 d6 4.O-O Nge7 5.Ng5 f6 6.Bf7+ Kd7 7.Qg4+ f5 8.exf5 h5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Paris Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T125","q":"125","title":"Trap 125","page":141,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkbnr/ppp2Bpp/2np4/4p3/3PP1b1/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","line":["Kxf7","c3"],"cp":273,"need":1,"lesson":"White sacrificed on f7 hoping to win Black's bishop, but forgot it was protected in a sneaky way. Black gave up the queen and took White's queen back, ending a piece ahead.","intro":"Paris Defense. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 d6 4.d4 Bg4 5.Bxf7+. Now find the zap!","opening":"Paris Defense","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T126","q":"126","title":"Trap 126","page":142,"type":"play","fen":"r3kb1r/pppq1Bpp/2np3n/4p1N1/4P1b1/1QP5/PP1P1PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 0 7","line":["Nxf7","Nxf7"],"cp":414,"need":1,"lesson":"White's queen and knight went on an early raid without enough support. Black took on f7 and then forked White's queen and knight with the bishop.","intro":"Paris Defense. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 d6 4.c3 Bg4 5.Qb3 Qd7 6.Ng5 Nh6 7.Bxf7+. Now find the zap!","opening":"Paris Defense","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T127","q":"127","title":"Trap 127","page":143,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk1nr/ppp2ppp/3p4/2b1p3/2BnP1b1/2NPBN2/PPP2PPP/R2Q1RK1 b kq - 5 7","line":["Bxf3","gxf3"],"cp":117,"alt":["Nxf3+","Nxf3+"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White had more pieces out but let Black's knight sit on the strong d4 square. Black traded on f3 to break open White's castled king and attacked it.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.d3 d6 5.O-O Bg4 6.Nc3 Nd4 7.Be3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T128","q":"128","title":"Trap 128","page":144,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/1pp2ppp/1pnp4/4N2n/2B1P3/3P4/PPPN1PPP/R2QR1K1 b - - 0 10","line":["Nxe5","d4"],"cp":421,"need":1,"lesson":"White thought the knight on h5 was loose and set a trap to win it. But Black recaptured with the knight, and when White's queen took on h5 it got trapped.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.d3 d6 5.O-O Nf6 6.Be3 Bb6 7.Bxb6 axb6 8.Nbd2 O-O 9.Re1 Nh5 10.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T129","q":"129","title":"Trap 129","page":145,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/pppp1pp1/2n3P1/2b1p3/2B1P3/2NP1N2/PPP2nP1/R2QK2R w KQ - 0 10","line":["Nxe5","Nxh1","Bxf7+","Rxf7","gxf7+","Kf8","Qh5","Nxe5","Qh8+","Kxf7","Qxd8","c6"],"cp":333,"need":3,"lesson":"Black greedily took the bishop with the h-pawn, which opened the h-file right at Black's own castled king. White's rook, pawns, and minor pieces swarmed in for mate.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.d3 O-O 6.Bg5 h6 7.h4 hxg5 8.hxg5 Ng4 9.g6 Nxf2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T130","q":"130","title":"Trap 130","page":146,"type":"play","fen":"r2q1rk1/ppp2ppp/3p1n2/2b1pPN1/1nB1P1b1/2NP4/PPPQ2PP/R1B1K2R b KQ - 0 9","line":["Be3","Qxe3","Nxc2+","Kf2","Nxe3","Bxe3","c6","h3","d5","exd5","Bxf5"],"cp":566,"need":5,"lesson":"White was so busy with his own plan to trap Black's bishop that he forgot to ask what Black was threatening. Black's knight fork on c2 won White's queen.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.d3 d6 6.Ng5 O-O 7.f4 Bg4 8.Qd2 Nb4 9.f5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T131","q":"131","title":"Trap 131","page":147,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/ppp2Np1/2np1n2/2b1p3/2B1P3/2NP2p1/PPP2PP1/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 0 10","line":["Nxe4","Nxh8","Qh4","Qh5+","Qxh5","Bf7+","Qxf7","Nxf7","gxf2+","Kh2","Nxc3","Nxd6+"],"cp":78,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White pushed the h-pawn and then took the bishop, opening the h-file right next to his own king. Pawns cannot move backward, so Black's rook and pieces poured in for mate.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.d3 d6 6.O-O Bg4 7.h3 h5 8.hxg4 hxg4 9.Ng5 g3 10.Nxf7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T132","q":"132","title":"Trap 132","page":148,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1r1k/ppp4p/2np1p1Q/2bNpp2/2B1P3/3P1N2/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 0 11","line":["Nh4","Be6","Ng6+","Kg8","exf5","hxg6"],"cp":825,"need":3,"lesson":"Black castled too early and let White pin his f6-Knight, so White smashed the pawns around his King. Black should have broken the pin or developed his light-square Bishop first.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Nc3 Nf6 5.d3 d6 6.Bg5 O-O 7.Nd5 Kh8 8.Bxf6 gxf6 9.Qd2 f5 10.Qh6 f6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T133","q":"133","title":"Trap 133","page":149,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/ppp2ppp/1bnp4/4p3/2BPP3/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 6","line":["dxe5","dxe5","Qxd8+","Nxd8","Nxe5","Be6","f4","c6","h3"],"cp":148,"alt":["Ng5"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black saved his Bishop but forgot about the e5-pawn, and after the trade one of his pieces had too many jobs to do. When a move attacks two things, make sure you deal with both threats.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Overload. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.c3 d6 5.d4 Bb6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Overload"},{"id":"T134","q":"134","title":"Trap 134","page":150,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2np1n2/8/1bBPP3/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQ1K1R w kq - 3 8","line":["d5","Ne5","Nxe5","dxe5"],"cp":257,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Bishop check did not help him, and the Bishop was left loose on b4 where a Queen check could fork it. Don't give pointless checks that leave your pieces unprotected.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.c3 d6 5.d4 exd4 6.cxd4 Bb4+ 7.Kf1 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T135","q":"135","title":"Trap 135","page":151,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/1pppqppp/pb3n2/4n1B1/1P2P3/2P2N2/P3BPPP/RN1QK2R b KQkq - 3 9","line":["Bxf2+","Kf1"],"cp":348,"need":1,"lesson":"White jumped around the board with moves that did not work together, leaving his f2-square and e4-pawn weak. Black turned the pin around with a Bishop sacrifice and a Knight fork.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.c3 Qe7 5.d4 Bb6 6.b4 a6 7.dxe5 Nxe5 8.Bg5 Nf6 9.Be2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T136","q":"136","title":"Trap 136","page":152,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqnrk1/pppp1ppp/1bn5/4P1N1/2BP4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 1 9","line":["Qd3","Qxg5"],"cp":713,"alt":["Qh5","Qh5"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black gave White a big pawn center, and the e-pawn chased his Knight away from f6, where it guarded his King. Black needed to fight for the center, for example with ...d5.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.c3 Nf6 5.d4 exd4 6.cxd4 Bb6 7.Ng5 O-O 8.e5 Ne8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T137","q":"137","title":"Trap 137","page":153,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/1b1P2nn/4P3/2B5/5N1P/PP3PP1/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 11","line":["Bg5","Qxg5","Nxg5","O-O","O-O","Re8","Nc3","Rxe5","Nce4","Re8","dxc7"],"cp":810,"need":3,"lesson":"Black let White's center pawns roll forward and push his pieces to the edge, where they got stuck. Black should have checked with ...Bb4+ instead of retreating to b6.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.c3 Nf6 5.d4 exd4 6.cxd4 Bb6 7.e5 Ng4 8.h3 Nh6 9.d5 Ne7 10.d6 Ng6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T138","q":"138","title":"Trap 138","page":154,"type":"play","fen":"r1b4Q/ppp2k1p/3p1np1/2P5/8/4B3/PPP2PqP/RN2KR2 b Q - 1 12","line":["Bh3","Qxf6+","Kxf6","Nd2","Qxh2","O-O-O","Bxf1","Nxf1","Qh1","cxd6","cxd6","Rxd6+"],"cp":432,"need":3,"lesson":"White grabbed a Rook but sent his Queen far away from his King, and then she got trapped in the corner. When your Queen goes hunting, make sure your King is still safe.","intro":"Giuoco Piano. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.Bxf7+ Kxf7 5.Nxe5+ Nxe5 6.Qh5+ g6 7.Qxe5 d6 8.Qxh8 Qh4 9.d4 Nf6 10.dxc5 Qxe4+ 11.Be3 Qxg2 12.Rf1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Giuoco Piano","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T139","q":"139","title":"Trap 139","page":155,"type":"playout","fen":"r2qk1nr/ppp2pp1/2np4/2b1p3/2B1P1p1/2P5/PB1P1PPN/RN1Q1RK1 b kq - 1 10","line":["Qh4","Bxf7+","Kd8","Bh5","Rxh5","Re1","Qxf2+","Kh1","Rxh2+","Kxh2","Qh4#"],"mate":6,"goal":"mate","lesson":"White never played d4 to take over the center, and taking the Bishop opened the h-file right in front of his own King. Black's Queen and Rook used that open file to give mate.","intro":"Evans Gambit. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.b4 Bxb4 5.c3 Bc5 6.O-O d6 7.Bb2 Bg4 8.h3 h5 9.hxg4 hxg4 10.Nh2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Evans Gambit","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T140","q":"140","title":"Trap 140","page":156,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp1ppp/1bn5/4P3/2B1n3/2P2N2/P4PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 9","line":["Qd5","O-O"],"cp":522,"need":1,"lesson":"Black put his Knight in the middle of the board with nothing protecting it while his King was still in the center. White's Queen attacked the loose Knight and the f7 mate square at the same time.","intro":"Evans Gambit. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.b4 Bxb4 5.c3 Bc5 6.O-O Nf6 7.d4 Bb6 8.dxe5 Nxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Evans Gambit","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T141","q":"141","title":"Trap 141","page":157,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp2p1/2n2n1p/b3P1B1/2B5/2P2N2/P4PPP/RN1QK2R w KQkq - 0 11","line":["exf6","gxf6","Be3","d5","Bxd5","Ne7","Qa4+","Qd7","Qxa5","Nxd5","O-O","Nxe3"],"cp":472,"need":1,"lesson":"Black's Knight on f6 kept getting chased by White's pawns until it had nowhere safe to go. Taking White's Bishop let White's pawn run all the way to the last rank.","intro":"Evans Gambit. Theme: Promotion. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.b4 Bxb4 5.c3 Ba5 6.d4 Nf6 7.dxe5 Ng4 8.Bg5 f6 9.exf6 Nxf6 10.e5 h6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Evans Gambit","tactic":"Promotion"},{"id":"T142","q":"142","title":"Trap 142","page":158,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/bppp1ppp/2n5/PB2p3/8/B4N2/2PPQnPP/RN2K2R w KQkq - 0 11","line":["Nxe5","Ne7"],"cp":7,"alt":["Bxc6"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black got greedy grabbing pawns with his Knight instead of castling, so his King stayed stuck in the center. White's Bishops and Knight lined up for discovered checks and mate.","intro":"Evans Gambit Declined. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Bc5 4.b4 Bb6 5.a4 a6 6.a5 Ba7 7.b5 axb5 8.Bxb5 Nf6 9.Ba3 Nxe4 10.Qe2 Nxf2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Evans Gambit Declined","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T143","q":"143","title":"Trap 143","page":159,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/ppp2ppp/5q2/2bBN3/3nn3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 b kq - 0 9","line":["Qxf2+","Kh1","Bf5","Bxe4","Bxe4","Rxe4","O-O-O","Nd3","Qxc2","Nc3","Qxd1+","Nxd1"],"cp":-147,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White opened lines to attack, but forgot about the weak f2-square next to his own King. Black's Queen and Knights jumped in and finished with a smothered-style Knight mate.","intro":"Two Knights Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.Re1 d5 6.Bb3 Bc5 7.d4 Nxd4 8.Nxe5 Qf6 9.Bxd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T144","q":"144","title":"Trap 144","page":160,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1b1r/pppp2kp/2N2np1/3Q4/8/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 1 10","line":["Bh6+","Kxh6"],"cp":523,"need":1,"lesson":"Black tried to be clever with an in-between move, but he forgot that White could give a check first. A checking Bishop sacrifice pulled his King out so White could win the Queen.","intro":"Two Knights Defense. Theme: In-Between Move. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.d4 exd4 5.Nxd4 Nxe4 6.Bxf7+ Kxf7 7.Qh5+ g6 8.Qd5+ Kg7 9.Nxc6 Nf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense","tactic":"In-Between Move"},{"id":"T145","q":"145","title":"Trap 145","page":161,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1bkr/ppp3pp/2np4/4P1N1/3p2Q1/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 0 9","line":["Qf3","Qe7"],"cp":466,"need":1,"lesson":"Black relaxed after taking the Bishop and let White's Knight sit on g5 next to the weak f7-square. He should have chased the Knight away with ...h6 before White's Queen joined it.","intro":"Two Knights Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.d4 exd4 5.e5 Ng4 6.Bxf7+ Kxf7 7.Ng5+ Kg8 8.Qxg4 d6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T146","q":"146","title":"Trap 146","page":162,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq2kr/pppp2pp/8/4n1N1/1b1p2n1/2P2Q2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R w KQ - 0 10","line":["Qd5+","Kf8","Ne6+","Ke8","Nxg7+","Kf8","Ne6+","Ke8","Nxd8","Kxd8","cxb4","Nd3+"],"cp":759,"need":3,"lesson":"Black captured on e5 with the wrong Knight, so his Queen on d8 lost her guard. After the check, White's Knight forked his King and Queen.","intro":"Two Knights Defense. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.d4 exd4 5.e5 Ng4 6.Bxf7+ Kxf7 7.Ng5+ Kg8 8.Qf3 Bb4+ 9.c3 Ncxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T147","q":"147","title":"Trap 147","page":163,"type":"play","fen":"r3k2r/ppp2ppp/2n1bq2/2b3N1/2pp4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 0 10","line":["Nxe6","fxe6","Qh5+","Kd7","Qxc5","Rhf8","Rf1","Qe7","Qxc4","Qb4","Nd2","Qxc4"],"cp":274,"need":5,"lesson":"Black was ahead in pawns, but his King was still stuck in the middle. A Queen check let White attack the King and the loose Bishop at the same time.","intro":"Two Knights Defense (Max Lange Attack). Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.d4 exd4 5.O-O Bc5 6.e5 d5 7.exf6 dxc4 8.Re1+ Be6 9.Ng5 Qxf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense (Max Lange Attack)","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T148","q":"148","title":"Trap 148","page":164,"type":"mate","fen":"r1b1k2N/ppp3pp/2np4/4p3/2B4q/8/PPPP3P/RNB2QKn w q - 0 11","line":["Qf7+","Kd8","Qf8+","Kd7","Be6+","Kxe6","Qf7#"],"mate":4,"need":7,"lesson":"In this wild opening both Kings are in danger, and Black took time out for a quiet move instead of keeping up the attack. That one slow move gave White time to chase his King to mate.","intro":"Two Knights Defense. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 Nf6 4.Ng5 Bc5 5.Nxf7 Bxf2+ 6.Kxf2 Nxe4+ 7.Kg1 Qh4 8.g3 Nxg3 9.Nxh8 Nxh1 10.Qf1 d6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Two Knights Defense","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T149","q":"149","title":"Trap 149","page":167,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp2ppp/2np4/1B2p3/3Pn3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 6","line":["d5","a6","Bd3","Ne7","Bxe4","f5","Bd3","Nxd5","Bc4"],"cp":284,"need":5,"lesson":"Black grabbed a pawn while his c6-Knight was pinned and his King was still in the center. He should have kept the position closed and castled first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.O-O Nf6 5.d4 Nxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T150","q":"150","title":"Trap 150","page":168,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkbnr/1pp2ppp/p1np4/4p3/B2PP1b1/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 b kq - 1 6","line":["b5","Bb3"],"cp":164,"need":1,"lesson":"White kept his Bishop pinning the Knight, but Black broke the pin with ...b5. Then Black's Knight took the d4-pawn because White's f3-Knight was pinned and could not help.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.O-O Bg4 5.d4 a6 6.Ba4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T151","q":"151","title":"Trap 151","page":169,"type":"play","fen":"r2q1rk1/ppp2pbp/2bp1np1/6B1/3NP3/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/2KR3R w - - 4 11","line":["Qd2","Bd7"],"cp":78,"alt":["f4","Nxc6"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black castled without noticing his f6-Knight was still pinned. He should have moved his Queen off the d8-h4 line first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.d4 Bd7 5.Nc3 Nf6 6.Bxc6 Bxc6 7.Qd3 exd4 8.Nxd4 g6 9.Bg5 Bg7 10.O-O-O O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T152","q":"152","title":"Trap 152","page":170,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/pppbnp1p/2np2p1/3N2B1/2BbP3/8/PPP2PPP/R2QK2R w KQkq - 0 10","line":["Bxe7","Qc8","Bf6","Bxf6","Nxf6+","Kf8","Qd2","Be6","Qh6+","Ke7","Nd5+","Bxd5"],"cp":189,"alt":["Qxd4"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black traded away his g7-Bishop, the piece that guarded the dark squares around his King. Without it, White's pieces moved onto f6 and h6 for mate.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.d4 Bd7 5.Nc3 Nge7 6.Bc4 exd4 7.Nxd4 g6 8.Bg5 Bg7 9.Nd5 Bxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T153","q":"153","title":"Trap 153","page":171,"type":"mate","fen":"3rkbnr/p1p2ppp/2p5/4N3/4P1b1/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQk - 0 8","line":["Rd1#"],"mate":1,"need":1,"lesson":"White grabbed a pawn with a Knight that was pinned, so it stopped guarding d1. Win a pawn if you can, but first check for your opponent's pins and threats.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.Bxc6+ bxc6 5.d4 Bg4 6.dxe5 dxe5 7.Qxd8+ Rxd8 8.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T154","q":"154","title":"Trap 154","page":172,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkb1r/1ppb2pp/p1np1p1n/4p3/2B1P3/2NP1N1P/PPP2PP1/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 2 8","line":["Bxh6","gxh6","Nh4","Qc8","Qh5+","Kd8","Qf7","Be7"],"cp":332,"need":3,"lesson":"Black pushed his f-pawn and put his Knight on h6, which opened lines straight to his King. Always watch out for open diagonals that lead to your King.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 d6 4.d3 Bd7 5.Nc3 f6 6.h3 a6 7.Bc4 Nh6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T155","q":"155","title":"Trap 155","page":173,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppppnppp/5n2/1B2N3/4P3/3P4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","line":["c6"],"cp":264,"need":1,"lesson":"White greedily grabbed a free pawn without asking why Black left it hanging. Black chased the Bishop and then forked the King and Knight with his Queen.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.d3 Ne7 5.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T156","q":"156","title":"Trap 156","page":174,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/1B2p3/4P3/3P1N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 5","line":["Bxc6","dxc6","Nxe5","Bc5","O-O","O-O","Nf3","Bg4","Nbd2","Re8","h3"],"cp":177,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's e5-pawn was only guarded by the c6-Knight, and White could trade the Bishop for it. Because White's e4-pawn was already protected, Black could not win the pawn back.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.d3 a6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T157","q":"157","title":"Trap 157","page":175,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp1b1pp/2pn4/4N3/8/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 1 10","line":["Bg5"],"cp":426,"need":1,"lesson":"Black pushed his f-pawn to protect e5, which opened the diagonal from h5 to his King. A Queen check then pinned his pawns and let White's Knight take for free.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.d4 f6 6.Re1 Nd6 7.Bxc6 dxc6 8.dxe5 fxe5 9.Nxe5 Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T158","q":"158","title":"Trap 158","page":176,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1pp2ppp/p1n5/3p4/2Ppn3/3B1N2/PP3PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["cxd5","Nxf2","Qe2+","Be7","dxc6","Nxd3","Qxd3","O-O","Qe4","f5","Qxd4"],"cp":272,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Knight on e4 was only held up by the d5-pawn. Once White removed that pawn, the Knight fell because Black's Queen could not take back on e4 without being pinned.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.d4 a6 6.Bd3 d5 7.c4 exd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T159","q":"159","title":"Trap 159","page":177,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppppn1pp/8/1B3p2/3Nn3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 1 8","line":["Rxe4","fxe4","Ne6","c6","Nxd8","cxb5","Nc3","Ng6","Qd5","Kxd8","Bg5+","Kc7"],"cp":666,"alt":["Ne6","Ne6"],"need":5,"lesson":"Black's Knight move blocked his own Queen in, and his d-pawn was pinned so it could not capture on e6. White's Knight jumped in and trapped the Queen.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.d4 exd4 6.Re1 f5 7.Nxd4 Ne7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T160","q":"160","title":"Trap 160","page":178,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/pppp2pp/2n5/1Bb2p2/3Nn3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 1 8","line":["Rxe4+","fxe4","Qh5+","g6","Qxc5","Qe7","Qc3","Qf6"],"cp":516,"need":3,"lesson":"Black opened the e-file, pushed his f-pawn and left his Bishop loose on c5. A Queen check then forked his King and that Bishop.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.d4 exd4 6.Re1 f5 7.Nxd4 Bc5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T161","q":"161","title":"Trap 161","page":179,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kb1r/2p2ppp/p1p2q2/3p2N1/3Qn3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1R1K1 w kq - 2 10","line":["Nxe4","dxe4"],"cp":165,"need":1,"lesson":"Black took White's d-pawn and kept his King in the center while the e-file was open. Then a discovered check from White's Rook led to mate.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.d4 exd4 6.Re1 d5 7.Qxd4 a6 8.Bxc6+ bxc6 9.Ng5 Qf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T162","q":"162","title":"Trap 162","page":180,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp2pp/2nn4/1B2pp2/8/3P1N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 1 7","line":["Bxc6","Be7","Bd5","e4","dxe4","fxe4","Nc3","c6","Nxe4","Nxe4","Bxe4","d5"],"cp":668,"need":1,"lesson":"Black tried too much, pushing his f-pawn and wasting time with his Knight. That weakened his King, and White won the Queen with a Knight fork.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.Re1 f5 6.d3 Nd6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T163","q":"163","title":"Trap 163","page":181,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n5/4N3/8/2n5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQR1K1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Nxc6+","Be7","Nxe7","Nxd1","Ng6+","Qe7","Nxe7","Kd8","Nxc8","Rxc8","Rxd1","Re8"],"cp":472,"need":1,"lesson":"Black grabbed pieces while his King was still sitting on the open e-file in front of White's Rook. When an enemy Rook lines up on your King, castle quickly instead of grabbing more.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Nxe4 5.Re1 Nd6 6.Nc3 Nxb5 7.Nxe5 Nxc3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T164","q":"164","title":"Trap 164","page":182,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2p2n2/2b1N3/4P3/3P4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 6","line":["Qd4","Be3"],"cp":389,"need":1,"lesson":"White grabbed the e5-pawn without seeing that Black's Queen could jump to d4, attacking the Knight and threatening mate on f2 at the same time. Before grabbing a pawn, check what the enemy Queen can attack after you take.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Bc5 4.d3 Nf6 5.Bxc6 dxc6 6.Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T165","q":"165","title":"Trap 165","page":183,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/pppb1ppp/2n5/1Bbn4/Q2p4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 2 9","line":["Qc4"],"cp":368,"need":1,"lesson":"Black protected his pinned Knight on c6 but left his Bishop on c5 and Knight on d5 both loose, so one Queen move attacked them both. Always check which of your pieces are unprotected before you answer a threat.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Bc5 4.c3 Nf6 5.d4 exd4 6.O-O d5 7.exd5 Nxd5 8.Qa4 Bd7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T166","q":"166","title":"Trap 166","page":184,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/ppppb1pp/8/1B2n1N1/4p3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 8","line":["Ne6","c6"],"cp":490,"need":1,"lesson":"Black took a pawn with his Knight, which left his d-pawn pinned and unable to guard e6. White's Knight jumped to e6 and trapped the Black Queen, so Black should have traded off that Knight first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Bc5 4.c3 f5 5.d4 fxe4 6.Ng5 Be7 7.dxe5 Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T167","q":"167","title":"Trap 167","page":185,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/ppppqppp/5n2/1B2Q3/3PP3/8/PPP2KPP/RNB4R b kq - 0 8","line":["Ng4+","Kf3"],"cp":719,"need":1,"lesson":"White brought his Queen out early and then grabbed a Knight, walking into a Knight fork of his King and Queen. Don't rush your Queen out without a plan, because it just becomes a target.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Bc5 4.Nxe5 Bxf2+ 5.Kxf2 Nxe5 6.Qh5 Qe7 7.d4 Nf6 8.Qxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T168","q":"168","title":"Trap 168","page":186,"type":"play","fen":"r1b2rk1/ppppqppp/1bn2n2/1B2p1B1/3PP3/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RN1Q1RK1 w - - 3 8","line":["Bxc6","dxc6","dxe5","h6","exf6","Qxe4","Nbd2","Qg6","Bh4","Be6","fxg7","Kxg7"],"cp":416,"need":5,"lesson":"Black guarded his e5-pawn with his Queen instead of a pawn, and his pinned Knight on f6 could not help. Black should have played ...d6, because a pawn is a much sturdier guard than a Queen.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Bc5 5.c3 O-O 6.d4 Bb6 7.Bg5 Qe7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T169","q":"169","title":"Trap 169","page":187,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/pppp1ppp/2n5/1Bb5/4P1nq/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQR1K1 b kq - 2 8","line":["Bxf2+","Kh1","Bxe1","Qxe1","Qxe1+","Nxe1","Nf2+","Kg1","Nxe4","Bf4","d6","Bxc6+"],"cp":392,"alt":["Qxf2+"],"need":3,"lesson":"White moved his Rook off f1, which left the f2-square weak, and Black's Queen and Knight crashed in for a smothered mate. Don't automatically play your Rook to e1 if it leaves f2 without protection.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Bc5 5.Re1 Ng4 6.d4 exd4 7.Nxd4 Qh4 8.Nf3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T170","q":"170","title":"Trap 170","page":188,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/ppp2ppp/2p5/2b1N3/8/8/PPPPQnPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Nd3+","Be7","Qxf2","O-O","Nc3","Be6","Nf4","Bf5","d3","Bd6","Ne4","Be5"],"cp":289,"need":3,"lesson":"Black greedily grabbed f2 while his King sat on the open e-file facing White's Queen, and White got to give the discovered check first. Black should have played ...Qd5 to keep things safe.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nf6 4.O-O Bc5 5.Bxc6 dxc6 6.Nxe5 Nxe4 7.Qe2 Nxf2. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T171","q":"171","title":"Trap 171","page":189,"type":"play","fen":"rnbqk2r/ppppn1pp/1b6/1B1Pp1N1/4p3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 2 9","line":["Ne6","c6","Nxd8","cxb5","Nf7","Kxf7","Nd2","Nxd5","Nxe4","Nf6","Nd6+","Kf8"],"cp":848,"need":3,"lesson":"Black wasted time moving the same pieces and pawns over and over, so White's Knight had time to reach e6 and trap the Black Queen. In the opening, develop new pieces instead of wasting moves.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Bc5 4.O-O Nge7 5.c3 f5 6.d4 Bb6 7.d5 fxe4 8.Ng5 Nb8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T172","q":"172","title":"Trap 172","page":190,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp2pp/8/4p3/2Bnp3/2N2N2/PPPP1PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 6","line":["Nxd4","Nf6","Nxe4","c6","Nb3","d5","Nxf6+","Qxf6","Be2","Be7","d4","O-O"],"cp":305,"need":1,"lesson":"Black's pawn capture opened the path from h5 to e5, so White's Queen could check the King and attack the Rook at the same time. When you push your f-pawn, watch out for Queen checks on the h5-e8 diagonal.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 f5 4.Nc3 Nd4 5.Bc4 fxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T173","q":"173","title":"Trap 173","page":191,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp2pp/5q2/1B2N3/3nNP2/8/PPPP2PP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 0 7","line":["Qxf4","Bd3","Qxe5","O-O","Ne7","Ng3","Qd5","Be4","Qe6","Bd3","d5","Kh1"],"cp":264,"need":3,"lesson":"White took a pawn with his Knight and let Black's Queen fork both White Knights and also attack the Bishop. White should have pulled his Knight back to f3 to stay safe.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 f5 4.Nc3 Nd4 5.Nxe5 Qf6 6.f4 fxe4 7.Nxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T174","q":"174","title":"Trap 174","page":192,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pppp3p/2n5/1B4p1/3Pp3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 9","line":["Qh5+","Ke7","Bxg5+","Kd6","Bxd8","Nxd4","Bf6","Nxc2+","Kd1","Ke6","Qe5+","Kf7"],"cp":1334,"need":5,"lesson":"Black took the Knight with a pawn, which opened the diagonal to his King and let White's Bishop skewer the King and Queen. Black should have recaptured with his Queen instead, and avoid weakening pawn moves near the King.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Skewer. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 f5 4.Nc3 fxe4 5.Nxe4 Nf6 6.Nxf6+ gxf6 7.d4 e4 8.Ng5 fxg5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Skewer"},{"id":"T175","q":"175","title":"Trap 175","page":193,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/ppp3pp/2p2n2/4N3/4p3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQ1RK1 b kq - 2 7","line":["Qd4","Nc4","Qxc4","d3","Qe6","Bg5","Be7","Re1","O-O","Nxe4","Qf7","Bxf6"],"cp":375,"need":3,"lesson":"White's Knight on e5 had no pawn supporting it, so Black's Queen attacked it and it had nowhere safe to go. White should have pushed his d-pawn to d4 to support the Knight.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 f5 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O fxe4 6.Nxe5 Nf6 7.Nc3. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T176","q":"176","title":"Trap 176","page":194,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppp3pp/2p5/4Np1Q/3qP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 2 6","line":["g6","Nxg6","hxg6","Qxg6+","Kd8","d3","Ne7","Qg3","fxe4","Nc3","exd3","cxd3"],"cp":280,"need":3,"lesson":"White gave a pointless check instead of moving his attacked Knight to safety, and ...g6 left both White pieces under attack. Don't give checks that only help your opponent; deal with your own problems first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 f5 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.Nxe5 Qd4 6.Qh5+. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T177","q":"177","title":"Trap 177","page":195,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk2r/pp2bppp/2p1b3/3n3Q/2Bp4/3P4/PPP2PPP/RNB1R1K1 w kq - 4 11","line":["Rxe6","g6","Qe5","Rf8","Rxe7+","Qxe7","Qxe7+","Nxe7","Nd2","O-O-O","Nf3","Nf5"],"cp":318,"need":1,"lesson":"Black got ready to castle but forgot his Bishop on e6 was pinned and needed more protection. Black should have played ...Qd7 to guard it, because a normal-looking developing move isn't always safe.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nd4 4.Nxd4 exd4 5.d3 c6 6.Bc4 Nf6 7.O-O d5 8.exd5 Nxd5 9.Re1+ Be6 10.Qh5 Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T178","q":"178","title":"Trap 178","page":196,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1ppp3p/p1n2pp1/4p2Q/4P2N/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Nxg6","hxg6","Qxh8","Nb4","Nc3","Nxc2","Nd5","Kf7","Rb1","c6","Nc3","d5"],"cp":341,"need":3,"lesson":"Black pushed his f-pawn, which weakened the squares around his King, and then recaptured with the wrong piece so g6 was not protected. Moves made without a plan leave your King open to a hunt.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: King Hunt. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nge7 4.O-O f6 5.Nh4 a6 6.Bxc6 Nxc6 7.Qh5+ g6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"King Hunt"},{"id":"T179","q":"179","title":"Trap 179","page":197,"type":"mate","fen":"r3qb1r/pppbk1p1/2np2np/4p2Q/2BPP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNB2RK1 w - - 4 11","line":["Bg5+","hxg5","Qxg5#"],"mate":2,"alt":["Qg5+","Qg5+"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black pushed ...h6, which weakened his Kingside and let White sacrifice on f7 and then finish with a criss-cross mate by the two Bishops. Be careful about pawn moves in front of your King in the opening.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nge7 4.c3 d6 5.d4 Bd7 6.O-O Ng6 7.Ng5 h6 8.Nxf7 Kxf7 9.Bc4+ Ke7 10.Qh5 Qe8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T180","q":"180","title":"Trap 180","page":198,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkb1r/2p1npp1/p2p3p/3Nn3/Pp2P1b1/1B3N2/1PP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 11","line":["Nxe5","Be6","Ng4","Nxd5","Bxd5","Be7","O-O","O-O","Ne3","Bxd5","Nxd5","Bf6"],"cp":571,"need":1,"lesson":"Black thought White's Knight was stuck in a pin, but White moved it anyway and gave up the Queen to force checkmate. Black should have recaptured on e5 with a pawn instead.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nge7 4.Nc3 a6 5.Ba4 b5 6.Bb3 h6 7.d4 d6 8.a4 b4 9.Nd5 Bg4 10.dxe5 Nxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T181","q":"181","title":"Trap 181","page":199,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2nppp/2p5/8/3Qp3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 9","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Qxd8","Nd5","Nc3","Nxc3","bxc3","Kg6","Qe8+","Kf5"],"cp":854,"need":3,"lesson":"Black's King had to guard both f7 and the Queen on d8, and White's Bishop check pulled the King away so the Queen fell. Black should have developed his pieces, like bringing the Knight to c6, before grabbing pawns.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Deflection. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 Nge7 4.d4 exd4 5.Nxd4 Nxd4 6.Qxd4 c6 7.Bc4 d5 8.Bb3 dxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Deflection"},{"id":"T182","q":"182","title":"Trap 182","page":200,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/1pp1nppp/p1n5/3q4/Bb1N4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 9","line":["Nxc6","Qxd1","Nxb4+","Qd7","Bxd7+","Bxd7","Re1","Be6","Nd3","Nc6","Be3","O-O-O"],"cp":450,"need":5,"lesson":"Black's King was still in the middle and his Knight on c6 was pinned by the Bishop on a4, so it could not be safely defended. Black should have broken the pin with ...b5 before opening the center.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Bb4 5.O-O Nge7 6.d4 exd4 7.Nxd4 d5 8.exd5 Qxd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T183","q":"183","title":"Trap 183","page":201,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/2p1n1pp/pbnp1p2/1p4N1/3PP3/1B6/PP3PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 11","line":["Nf7","Qd7"],"cp":732,"alt":["Qh5+"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black put his Knight on e7 instead of f6, so nothing guarded h5 and White's Queen jumped in. Knights usually belong on the third row, like f6, where they defend the King better.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 b5 5.Bb3 Bc5 6.O-O Nge7 7.c3 d6 8.d4 exd4 9.cxd4 Bb6 10.Ng5 f6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T184","q":"184","title":"Trap 184","page":202,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/2pp1ppp/pb3n2/1p2n3/3PP3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 1 9","line":["dxe5","O-O","exf6","Qxf6","Nc3","Bb7","a4","Bc6","Nd5","Qe5","Nxb6","cxb6"],"cp":502,"need":1,"lesson":"Black let White's d-pawn fork his pieces and push his Knight away, and then White's Queen attacked the Rook and f7 at once. Black should have taken on d4 with his Bishop instead of retreating.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Double Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 b5 5.Bb3 Bc5 6.O-O Nf6 7.Nxe5 Nxe5 8.d4 Bb6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Double Attack"},{"id":"T185","q":"185","title":"Trap 185","page":203,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/2pp1ppp/p4n2/1p2b3/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 10","line":["f4","Bd6","e5","Bc5+","Kh1","O-O","exf6","Qxf6","f5","Bb7","Nc3"],"cp":349,"need":3,"lesson":"Black put his Bishop on c5 too early and fell for the fork trick, then his pieces got chased around. When you push ...b5 in the Ruy Lopez, watch out for tricks along the long light-square diagonal.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 b5 5.Bb3 Bc5 6.O-O Nf6 7.Nxe5 Nxe5 8.d4 Bd6 9.dxe5 Bxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T186","q":"186","title":"Trap 186","page":204,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkbnr/1bpp1ppp/p7/1p2p3/3nP3/1B3N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Nxe5+","Ke8","Qxd4","Nf6","Nc3","c5","Qe3","b4","Ne2","Bxe4"],"cp":53,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black tried to win a pawn with ...Nxd4, but White's Bishop sacrifice on f7 removed the King's guard and won back more. Black should have played the calm ...d6 or ...exd4 instead.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 b5 5.Bb3 Bb7 6.d4 Nxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T187","q":"187","title":"Trap 187","page":205,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkbnr/2p2ppp/p2p4/1p6/3QP3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 0 8","line":["c5","Qe3"],"cp":283,"need":1,"lesson":"White recaptured with his Queen, which let Black chase it with pawns and trap White's Bishop on b3 (the Noah's Ark Trap). White should have first played an in-between move like Bd5 before taking back on d4.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 d6 5.d4 b5 6.Bb3 Nxd4 7.Nxd4 exd4 8.Qxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T188","q":"188","title":"Trap 188","page":206,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkbnr/2p1n1pp/p7/1p1pP1N1/4p3/1BP5/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 10","line":["O-O","Nh6"],"cp":343,"alt":["Nxe4"],"need":1,"lesson":"Black's pawn on d5 was guarding his Queen's file, so when it took White's Knight, a Bishop check pulled the King away and the Queen fell. Black should have taken on e4 earlier with ...dxe4 instead of pushing ...b5.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Deflection. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 d6 5.c3 f5 6.d4 fxe4 7.Ng5 b5 8.Bb3 d5 9.dxe5 Nce7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Deflection"},{"id":"T189","q":"189","title":"Trap 189","page":207,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1kb1N/1pp4p/p1p5/5p2/3qP1nQ/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K2R b KQq - 0 10","line":["Qxe4+","Kd1","Ne3+","dxe3","Qxh4","Nc3","Qxf2"],"cp":714,"need":5,"lesson":"White grabbed the Rook in the corner but left his Queen on h4 lined up behind Black's Knight, so a discovered attack won it. White's Queen should have retreated to h3, out of the line of fire.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 f5 5.Bxc6 dxc6 6.Nxe5 Qd4 7.Qh5+ g6 8.Nxg6 Nf6 9.Qh4 Ng4 10.Nxh8. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"},{"id":"T190","q":"190","title":"Trap 190","page":208,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/2p2ppp/p1n2n2/1pbpp3/4P3/2P2N2/PPBPQPPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq d6 0 8","line":["exd5","Ne7","Nxe5","Qxd5","O-O","Bb7","Nf3","Qe6","Qxe6","fxe6","d4","Bd6"],"cp":156,"need":3,"lesson":"Black opened the center with ...d5 before castling, and White's pieces attacked his loose pawn and Knights. Don't open the center until your King is safely castled.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.Qe2 Bc5 6.c3 b5 7.Bc2 d5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T191","q":"191","title":"Trap 191","page":209,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/2p2ppp/p1np1n2/1p6/3NP3/1BN5/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 0 8","line":["Nxd4","Qxd4","c5","Qd2","c4","O-O","cxb3","axb3","Bb7","Qe3","Be7","Rd1"],"cp":305,"need":3,"lesson":"White's light-square Bishop on b3 got surrounded by Black's pawns, and White had several chances to save it but didn't. Watch out for the Noah's Ark Trap, where pawns box in your Bishop.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Trapped Piece. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.Nc3 d6 6.d4 b5 7.Bb3 exd4 8.Nxd4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Trapped Piece"},{"id":"T192","q":"192","title":"Trap 192","page":210,"type":"play","fen":"r1b1k2r/1ppp1ppp/p4q2/2b1n3/B3Q3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 1 9","line":["d4","Bxd4","c3","Bb6","Bf4","O-O","Qxe5","Qxe5","Bxe5","Re8","Bf4","Re2"],"cp":198,"alt":["Nc3"],"need":3,"lesson":"Black's Knight on e5 was pinned to his King by White's Queen, and White kept piling up on it until it fell. Black should have played ...Qe7 to break the pin right away.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.O-O Bc5 6.Nxe5 Nxe4 7.Qe2 Nxe5 8.Qxe4 Qf6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T193","q":"193","title":"Trap 193","page":211,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk2r/2p1bppp/p1n5/P2pp3/1p1Pn3/1B3N2/1PP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 1 10","line":["dxe5","Nc5","Bxd5","Bb7","Be3","O-O","c3","Ne6","Ra4","Qc8","Bc1","h6"],"cp":185,"need":3,"lesson":"Black ignored White's threats on the light squares, and White's Bishop pinned his Knight on c6 to win a piece. After opening the center, you have to be ready for the attack of the better-developed side.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.O-O Nxe4 6.d4 b5 7.Bb3 d5 8.a4 b4 9.a5 Be7. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T194","q":"194","title":"Trap 194","page":212,"type":"play","fen":"r2qkb1r/2p2ppp/p4n2/np2p3/4P1b1/1B3N2/PPP1QPPP/RNB2RK1 w kq - 0 10","line":["Bxf7+","Kxf7","Nxe5+","Kg8","Nxg4","h5","Nxf6+","gxf6","a4","b4","e5","Qe7"],"cp":352,"need":5,"lesson":"Black thought his Bishop's pin on the f3-Knight was strong, but a Bishop sacrifice on f7 broke it and the Knight forked the King and Bishop. Black should have stuck with his plan of trading off White's Bishop first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.O-O d6 6.Qe2 b5 7.Bb3 Na5 8.d4 Bg4 9.dxe5 dxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T195","q":"195","title":"Trap 195","page":213,"type":"play","fen":"r1bq1rk1/1pppbppp/p1n2n2/4p3/B3P3/5N2/PPPPQPPP/RNB2RK1 w - - 6 7","line":["Bxc6","dxc6","h3","h6","d3","Qd6","Nc3","Re8"],"cp":37,"alt":["c3"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black castled instead of guarding his e-pawn, so White traded off the Knight protecting it and won the pawn. Black should have defended e5 with ...d6 or chased White's Bishop with ...b5 first.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Removing the Guard. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Ba4 Nf6 5.O-O Be7 6.Qe2 O-O. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Removing the Guard"},{"id":"T196","q":"196","title":"Trap 196","page":214,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/1pp3pp/p1p2p2/2b5/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 1 8","line":["Qh5+","g6","Qxc5","Qd6","Qc3","h5","Nf3","Be6","Be3","Qe7","Nbd2","O-O-O"],"cp":625,"need":3,"lesson":"Playing ...f6 opened a diagonal toward Black's King, and then Black put his Bishop where White's Queen could check and grab it at the same time. Black should have chased the Knight with ...c5 first to make it safe.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O f6 6.d4 exd4 7.Nxd4 Bc5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T197","q":"197","title":"Trap 197","page":215,"type":"mate","fen":"r2qkbnr/1pp2pp1/p1p5/4p3/4P1p1/8/PPPP1PP1/RNBQNRK1 b kq - 1 8","line":["Qh4","f4","g3","Qh5","Rxh5","fxe5","Qh1#"],"mate":4,"need":7,"lesson":"White grabbed the free Bishop, but that opened the h-file right at his own King. He should have kept developing his pieces until taking on g4 was safe.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Mating Attack. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O Bg4 6.h3 h5 7.hxg4 hxg4 8.Ne1. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Mating Attack"},{"id":"T198","q":"198","title":"Trap 198","page":216,"type":"play","fen":"r3kbnr/1pp2ppp/p1p5/3qN3/4b1P1/7P/PPPP1P2/RNBQR1K1 w kq - 2 10","line":["Nc3","Qe6","Nxe4","h6","Ng3","O-O-O","d4","Kb8","c3","Qd5","a4","Nf6"],"cp":551,"need":3,"lesson":"Black grabbed a pawn while his King was still stuck on the open e-file. White's Rook lined up on that file and pinned Black's Queen to his King. Black should have traded his Bishop for the f3-Knight instead of backing it away.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O Bg4 6.h3 Bh5 7.g4 Bg6 8.Nxe5 Bxe4 9.Re1 Qd5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T199","q":"199","title":"Trap 199","page":217,"type":"play","fen":"r2qk1nr/1pp2ppp/p1p5/4b3/4P1b1/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Qxd8+","Rxd8","Nxe5","Be2","Re1","Rd1","Rxd1","Bxd1","Na3","h6","Be3"],"cp":537,"need":3,"lesson":"Black thought his pin on the f3-Knight protected his Bishop. Once the Queens were traded, the pin was gone. Black should have traded Bishop for Knight on f3 before taking back on e5.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Unpin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O Bd6 6.d4 Bg4 7.dxe5 Bxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Unpin"},{"id":"T200","q":"200","title":"Trap 200","page":218,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqk1nr/1pp3pp/p1pb4/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNBQ1RK1 w kq - 0 8","line":["Nxe5","Nf6"],"cp":161,"need":1,"lesson":"Playing ...f6 at the wrong moment opened the diagonal to Black's King, so White could give up a Knight and get it back with a Queen check that forks King and Bishop. Timing matters: the same move can be fine one turn and a mistake the next.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Fork. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.O-O Bd6 6.d4 f6 7.dxe5 fxe5. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Fork"},{"id":"T201","q":"201","title":"Trap 201","page":219,"type":"play","fen":"r1bqkb1r/1pp2ppp/p1p5/4N3/3Pn3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 7","line":["O-O","Be7","Re1","Nd6","Nc3","O-O","b3","Re8","Bf4","Bf5","d5","Bf6"],"cp":25,"alt":["Qe2"],"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"Black let his e-pawn go and then took White's e-pawn, leaving his Knight stuck on the open e-file in front of his King. He should have traded pawns with 5...exd4 instead.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Pin. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 dxc6 5.d4 Nf6 6.Nxe5 Nxe4. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Pin"},{"id":"T202","q":"202","title":"Trap 202","page":220,"type":"play","fen":"r3kbnr/1bpp1ppp/p1p1P1q1/8/3Q4/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNB2RK1 b kq - 0 9","line":["Bd6","exd7+","Kf8","Ne5","Qe6","Re1","c5","Qe3","Nf6"],"cp":-77,"need":1,"strategy":true,"lesson":"White threw his e-pawn forward too quickly, and Black's pieces were aimed right at White's King. He should have kept calm and developed with Nc3 or Nbd2 instead of attacking too early.","intro":"Ruy Lopez. Theme: Discovery. The game went 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bb5 a6 4.Bxc6 bxc6 5.d4 exd4 6.Qxd4 Qf6 7.e5 Qg6 8.O-O Bb7 9.e6. Now find the zap!","opening":"Ruy Lopez","tactic":"Discovery"}]});
